{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0157dxZrLB6Lz4rgJm5NNsAm","type":"tool_result","content":"800\tthe player answers the Overclock. Pyro columns fire on every score (cosmetic, with light flashes).\n801\t\n802\t### 10.2 Teams and players\n803\t\n804\tRatings in the order ZOOM / SPLASH / DEEP / SLAM / DIME / SWIPE / SWAT / BUMP.\n805\t\n806\t| Team | Colors (jersey / trim / shorts) | Logo | Style |\n807\t|---|---|---|---|\n808\t| NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS | `#ff3ca6` / `#2de2ff` / `#1a1420` | a winged sneaker | flashy, fast, high-flying |\n809\t| BOARDWALK BREAKERS | `#18c8b8` / `#ff7a5c` / `#f2d8a0` | a breaking wave | passing and threes |\n810\t| SCRAPYARD CRUSHERS | `#d8641e` / `#ffd23a` / `#1c1a18` | crossed wrenches | power and steals |\n811\t| KABOOM MAGMA | `#ff3a1a` / `#ffb020` / `#22181e` | a volcano erupting a basketball | defense and clutch shooting |\n812\t| THE BLAMBOTS (boss; unlocked by the Tour) | `#c8d0dc` / `#e8c040` / `#3a4250` | a robot fist holding a ball | everything, loudly |\n813\t| CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS (secret; unlocked by the Tour) | `#f4f0ea` / `#ffc83a` / `#4a2a8a` | the Channel BLAM microphone | showbiz |\n814\t\n815\t| Player | Team | Role | Build, size | Look | Ratings | Voice | Taunt |\n816\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n817\t| VOLT | Hightops | high-flyer | heroic 1.65 | electric-blue ponytail, magenta band, skin `#8a5a3c` | 9 5 4 9 6 6 4 3 | bright, quick, 220 Hz | raise the roof |\n818\t| BIG RUMBLE | Hightops | enforcer | bulky 1.9 | black flattop, cyan wristbands, skin `#4a2c1e` | 3 3 1 7 4 4 9 10 | deep, slow, 85 Hz | flex |\n819\t| PIXEL | Hightops | sharpshooter | heroic 1.55 | green spiky hair, shades, skin `#f0c8a0` | 6 9 9 3 7 5 3 3 | squeaky, 270 Hz | finger guns |\n820\t| RIPTIDE | Breakers | point guard | heroic 1.6 | long sun-bleached hair, skin `#d8a070` | 10 6 6 5 10 7 2 3 | laid-back drawl, 170 Hz | surf balance |\n821\t| SHELLSHOCK | Breakers | three-point bomber | heroic 1.65 | coral afro, skin `#6a4028` | 6 8 10 3 6 5 3 4 | sing-song, 200 Hz | goggles (hands circle the eyes) |\n822\t| LONGBOARD | Breakers | shot blocker | heroic 1.85, legs × 1.12 | bald, teal band, skin `#c89070` | 4 5 2 7 4 3 9 7 | slow, 120 Hz | finger wag |\n823\t| TORQUE | Crushers | power dunker | bulky 1.85 | black mohawk, skin `#c8a080` | 6 4 2 10 4 4 6 9 | gravel, 95 Hz (noise in it) | chest pound |\n824\t| SPARKPLUG | Crushers | pickpocket | chibi 1.65 | yellow cap, skin `#3a2418` | 9 6 6 4 7 10 2 2 | fast, 300 Hz | shimmy |\n825\t| HUBCAP | Crushers | veteran all-rounder | heroic 1.7 | short grey hair, skin `#e0b090` | 5 7 6 6 6 6 6 6 | grumpy, 130 Hz | taps an imaginary watch |\n826\t| OBSIDIAN | Magma | rim protector | bulky 1.95 | bald, skin `#3a2216` | 4 4 1 8 3 4 10 8 | rumbling, 78 Hz | arms crossed, stone face |\n827\t| EMBER | Magma | clutch shooter | heroic 1.6 | long red hair, skin `#f0c090` | 7 9 8 5 6 6 3 3 | crisp, 230 Hz | blows on fingertips |\n828\t| PUMICE | Magma | leaper | heroic 1.65 | black afro, skin `#8a5030` | 8 5 3 9 5 5 7 3 | bouncy, 190 Hz | pogo hops |\n829\t| DUNKATRON | Blambots | destroyer | bulky 1.95, chrome helmet, red eye glow | chrome body, gold trim | 8 6 4 10 6 8 8 8 | robot, 95 Hz | robot dance |\n830\t| SWATBOT | Blambots | wall | bulky 1.95, same | chrome, red visor | 6 7 7 7 7 9 10 9 | robot, 120 Hz | \"processing\" head tilt |\n831\t| SPARE PARTS | Blambots | bench unit | bulky 1.8, same | mismatched panels | 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 | glitchy robot, 150 Hz | glitch wave |\n832\t| VINNIE VOX | All-Stars | play-by-play man | heroic 1.7 | headset band, skin `#e8b890` | 5 7 7 5 8 5 4 5 | the announcer (low) | mic drop |\n833\t| DEE DEE DECIBEL | All-Stars | color commentator | heroic 1.6 | purple ponytail, skin `#6a4030` | 7 8 6 6 7 6 5 4 | the announcer (high) | points at the camera |\n834\t| BLAMMO | All-Stars | the league's gorilla mascot | bulky 2.0, hunch .2 | dark fur (skin and hair `#3a2e2a`), lighter face | 7 3 1 10 3 6 9 10 | gorilla | chest drum |\n835\t\n836\tStory characters (not playable): **COMMISSIONER GIGAWATT** (CEO of GLOBO-BLAM Corp; heroic 1.6, purple coat, gold belt,\n837\twhite hair, a smug smile; a nasal, slow voice), **REF ROSCOE** (referee; white shirt with black trim, black cap, a\n838\twhistle; tosses the tip-off), **INTERN 1 and INTERN 2** (Blam Camp partners in grey practice jerseys), the **cleaning\n839\tbot** (a small metal Blob that replaces shattered glass). Vinnie and Dee Dee also appear at the studio desk in suits\n840\t(`outfit: 'coat'`). Every line about a player uses the player's NAME, never a pronoun, so any line fits any player.\n841\t\n842\t### 10.3 Dunk catalog (`06-data-moves.js`)\n843\t\n844\t| Id | Banner | Needs | Distance from rim | Choreography (u = flight progress) | Style bonus |\n845\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n846\t| `hammer` | TWO-HAND HAMMER | any | 0–70 | both hands raise the ball overhead from takeoff; slam at u .9 | 0 |\n847\t| `tomahawk` | TOMAHAWK! | SLAM 5 | 30–130 | ball in the right hand cocked far behind the head (u .3–.7), whipped forward at .88 | 50 |\n848\t| `doublepump` | DOUBLE PUMP! | SLAM 6 | 30–120 | ball pumped to the waist and back up twice (u .3, .55) | 80 |\n849\t| `reverse` | REVERSE ROCKET! | SLAM 6, approach within 50° of the baseline | 20–100 | turns its back to the rim mid-flight, slams backward over the head | 100 |\n850\t| `windmill` | WINDMILL! | SLAM 7 | 50–150 | right arm circles once (down past the hip, back, over the top) | 100 |\n851\t| `threesixty` | THREE-SIXTY! | SLAM 7 | 40–140 | facing turns 2π over u .2–.85; two-hand slam | 120 |\n852\t| `ftflyer` | FREE-THROW FLYER! | SLAM 8 | 110 to the dunk range | a long glide (apex + 30), legs split, one-hand slam | 150 |\n853\t| `flip` | FRONT-FLIP FREAK! | SLAM 8 | 60–150 | `flip` 0 → 1 over u .25–.75 (a front somersault), two-hand slam | 180 |\n854\t| `rattler` | RIM RATTLER! | SLAM 4 | 0–60 | two-hand slam, then `hang` 1.2 s with legs swinging | 60 |\n855\t| `nova720` | SEVEN-TWENTY SUPERNOVA! | Supernova | 60–190 | facing turns 4π, star-fire trail | 250 |\n856\t| `volcano` | VOLCANO LAUNCH! | a steam vent | from the vent | launched (apex 160), a 2π spin, a fireball slam; shatters 20% | 300 |\n857\t| `quake` | BLAM-QUAKE!!! | overclocked BLAMBOT; Moon Shoes 50%; Supernova 15% | 80 to the dunk range | huge apex, both hands, always shatters, the landing's shockwave knocks down everyone within 40 | 400 |\n858\t\n859\tChoice: every dunk whose needs pass, weighted by its bonus and by (SLAM − its minimum + 1), drawn with `S.rng`; the\n860\tsame for humans and the CPU. Each has an announcer line family (power, spin, flip, hang, long, nova, volcano, quake).\n861\t\n862\t### 10.4 Power-up icons\n863\t\n864\t12×12 string sprites, drawn bobbing above a pulsing floor ring in their color: ROCKET KICKS (a sneaker with a flame),\n865\tGLUE GLOVES (a green dripping glove), LASER SIGHT (a red crosshair), MOON SHOES (a spring shoe), BLAM BOMB (a black bomb\n866\twith a lit fuse), GOLD BALL (a gold ball with a shine). The same icons show on the players' plates with a countdown.\n867\t\n868\t### 10.5 The Blam Tour\n869\t\n870\tPROLOGUE → STOP 1 → STOP 2 → STOP 3 → THE REVEAL → THE FINAL → ENDING → CREDITS → HALL OF BLAM ENTRY.\n871\t\n872\t| You pick | Stop 1 | Stop 2 | Stop 3 | Final |\n873\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n874\t| Hightops | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n875\t| Breakers | Hightops at the Skybox | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n876\t| Crushers | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n877\t| Magma | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n878\t\n879\t- CPU difficulty: the Settings value (default Pro) shifted by stop: stop 1 one step lower, stop 2 as set, stop 3 half a\n880\t  step higher, the final one step higher (clamped to BLAM).\n881\t- Power-ups off at stop 1, on from stop 2. Quarters 1:30. One or two players (a second human joins on the same team at\n882\t  the Tour's team select).\n883\t- Each stop: tour map → matchup card (codes) → pre-game talk → tip-off → the game → results → post-game beat → map\n884\t  (autosave). A loss: results → REMATCH? 10-second countdown (Rematch, Tour Map, Quit Tour); a rematch replays the stop.\n885\t- Tour score = the stops' style points (wins only). At the end, or on quitting after a loss, a qualifying score enters\n886\t  the Hall of Blam (`E.Arcade` initials wheel).\n887\t\n888\t### 10.6 Story script (`04-data-story.js`)\n889\t\n890\tTone: a loud 90s sports broadcast. Announcers speak in ALL CAPS, punchy, pun-heavy; the Commissioner is smug and speaks\n891\tin sentence case; robots speak in SPACED. CAPITAL. WORDS. `{TEAM}` is your team's name; `{CAPTAIN}` your first player.\n892\tBeats play in engine scenes (§11.3) as `E.Dialog` lines with live portraits and voices, staged with posed rigs and camera\n893\tmoves (`game.script`, `game.tween`). Hold confirm 1 s to skip a beat, Start to skip all of it.\n894\t\n895\t1. **prologue** (the Channel BLAM studio desk; the Commissioner on a monitor)\n896\t   - VINNIE: \"GOOD EVENING, BALL FANS! LIVE FROM THE TOP OF THE WORLD, THIS IS CHANNEL BLAM!\"\n897\t   - DEE DEE: \"AND THIS IS THE BLAM TOUR! FIVE COURTS! FOUR CREWS! ONE GOLDEN BLAMBOOZLE! ZERO FOULS!\"\n898\t   - VINNIE: \"TONIGHT'S TOUR IS SPONSORED BY GLOBO-BLAM CORP. THEY MAKE EVERYTHING. THEY MADE THIS SENTENCE.\"\n899\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Greetings, little ballers. Win my Tour and the Golden Blamboozle is yours.\"\n900\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Lose, and your court becomes a GLOBO-BLAM parking lot. Validated parking, of course. Ha. Ha. Ha.\"\n901\t   - DEE DEE: \"{TEAM}, THE WHOLE CITY IS WATCHING. NO PRESSURE! EXCEPT ALL OF IT!\"\n902\t2. **camp-offer** (first Tour only) — DEE DEE: \"FIRST TIME ON THE TOUR? HIT BLAM CAMP AND I'LL SHOW YOU THE ROPES. OR\n903\t   DON'T. LIVE DANGEROUSLY!\" Choices: BLAM CAMP / LET'S PLAY.\n904\t3. **stop intro** (each stop, at the court) — VINNIE: \"STOP {N} OF THE BLAM TOUR: {HOME} VERSUS {AWAY} AT {COURT}!\" plus\n905\t   DEE DEE's court line: Skybox \"THIRTY STORIES UP AND THE NETS ARE STILL SMOKING!\"; Pier \"WATCH THE WIND, FOLKS. AND THE\n906\t   SEAGULLS. MOSTLY THE SEAGULLS.\"; Scrapyard \"OIL ON THE FLOOR AND FIRE IN THEIR EYES!\"; Caldera \"THE FLOOR IS HOT, THE\n907\t   VOLCANO IS HOTTER, AND THE MUSIC IS HOTTEST!\"; Dome \"THE BLAM DOME! SIXTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE VERY NERVOUS\n908\t   JUMBOTRON!\"\n909\t4. **pre-game talk** (the rival captain, then your captain's reply by team):\n910\t   - vs Breakers — RIPTIDE: \"Hope you packed sunscreen, {TEAM}. The tide's coming in, and it doesn't knock.\" Replies:\n911\t     VOLT \"Cute pier. I'm about to dunk on it.\" · TORQUE \"I've crushed bigger boats than this.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Sand turns\n912\t     to glass when I'm around.\"\n913\t   - vs Hightops — VOLT: \"Welcome to the Skybox. Try not to look down. Actually, look down: that's where you'll be.\"\n914\t     Replies: RIPTIDE \"Whoa, relax. We're just here to ride the wave. Over you.\" · TORQUE \"Fancy lights. They'll look\n915\t     great on my scrap pile.\" · EMBER \"Neon's cute. Lava's hotter.\"\n916\t   - vs Crushers — TORQUE: \"We crush cars for breakfast. You look like a light snack.\" Replies: VOLT \"Then you're about\n917\t     to get a stomachache.\" · SHELLSHOCK \"Careful, the floor's greasier than your jokes.\" · PUMICE \"I bounce. You crush.\n918\t     Let's see who's still standing.\"\n919\t   - vs Magma — OBSIDIAN: \"On Kaboom Island the floor is lava. Not a game. Actual lava. Walk carefully.\" Replies:\n920\t     BIG RUMBLE \"I don't walk carefully. I walk LOUD.\" · RIPTIDE \"Dude. Is that, like, safe?\" · SPARKPLUG \"I'm too fast\n921\t     to get burned!\"\n922\t5. **post-game, stop 1** — the beaten captain: RIPTIDE \"Wipeout. Totally gnarly, though. Respect.\" · VOLT \"Okay, okay.\n923\t   You can ball. Don't let it go to your head.\" · TORQUE \"You crushed us. That's MY job.\" · OBSIDIAN \"The mountain...\n924\t   respects you.\" Then GIGAWATT (monitor): \"Hmm. Promising. My engineers are taking notes. Lots of notes.\"\n925\t6. **post-game, stop 2** — GIGAWATT: \"Data received. Prototype calibration at ninety-eight percent. Keep playing,\n926\t   little ballers. Keep... teaching them.\" DEE DEE: \"TEACHING WHO? VINNIE, WHY DOES THE GLOBO-BLAM LOGO HAVE A ROBOT\n927\t   ARM?\" VINNIE: \"THAT'S BRANDING, DEE DEE. WE DON'T ASK QUESTIONS ON LIVE TV.\"\n928\t7. **the reveal** (after stop 3, at the Dome, the Commissioner in person)\n929\t   - VINNIE: \"THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!\"\n930\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Congratulations. You have earned the privilege... of being replaced.\"\n931\t   - GIGAWATT: \"Behold the future of basketball: the BLAMBOTS! No salaries! No sweat! No mercy!\"\n932\t   - DUNKATRON: \"BEEP. YOUR. CAREER. IS. DEPRECATED.\"\n933\t   - SWATBOT: \"INITIATING. TRASH. TALK. PROTOCOL. ... YOU. STINK.\"\n934\t   - {CAPTAIN} by team: VOLT \"Did the toaster just trash-talk me?\" · RIPTIDE \"Bummer. I was gonna say we could be\n935\t     friends.\" · TORQUE \"I've got a crusher with your names on it.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Metal melts.\"\n936\t8. **final pre-game** — VINNIE: \"THE FINAL! HUMANS VERSUS HARDWARE! THE BLAMBOOZLE IS ON THE LINE!\"\n937\t9. **overclock** (in play, captions and the jumbotron) — GIGAWATT: \"OVERCLOCK THEM! MAXIMUM BLAM!\" DEE DEE: \"THE ROBOTS\n938\t   ARE GLOWING! IS THAT LEGAL? THERE ARE NO RULES! I FORGOT!\"\n939\t10. **first reboot** (in play, once) — DEE DEE: \"THEY SHORT-CIRCUIT WHEN YOU KNOCK THEM DOWN! KEEP SHOVING, {TEAM}!\"\n940\t11. **ending** (after winning the final)\n941\t    - DUNKATRON: \"ERROR. ERROR. HUMANS. TOO. ... BLAM.\" (sparks; both bots topple)\n942\t    - VINNIE: \"THEY DID IT! {TEAM} WINS THE BLAM TOUR!\"\n943\t    - DEE DEE: \"AND THE BLAMBOTS ARE BEING RECYCLED INTO VERY SAD TOASTERS!\"\n944\t    - GIGAWATT: \"This isn't over! I'll buy another league! I'll buy the MOON! Hey! Put me down!\" (BLAMMO carries the\n945\t      Commissioner off over a shoulder)\n946\t    - VINNIE: \"STREETBALL IS SAVED! THE BLAMBOOZLE GOES HOME WITH {TEAM}!\"\n947\t    - DEE DEE: \"GOODNIGHT, EVERYBODY! REMEMBER: NO FOULS! NO MERCY!\" VINNIE and DEE DEE: \"ALL BLAM!\"\n948\t12. **credits** — scrolling credits over the trophy lift and a crowd confetti storm, the `credits` song; then unlock\n949\t    cards: \"UNLOCKED: THE BLAMBOTS\", \"UNLOCKED: CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS\", \"UNLOCKED: BIG HEADS (OPTIONS)\", \"SECRETS ON\n950\t    THE ABOUT SCREEN\".\n951\t13. **losses** — stops 1–3: GIGAWATT \"Tsk. Another court for my parking empire.\" The final: GIGAWATT \"Resistance is...\n952\t    adorable.\" DUNKATRON \"GAME. OVER. INSERT. COIN.\"\n953\t14. **halftime gags** (one per halftime, no repeats within a Tour): \"THIS HALFTIME IS BROUGHT TO YOU BY GLOBO-BLAM\n954\t    SNEAKER GLUE. STICK THE LANDING. FOREVER.\" · \"OUR STATS DEPARTMENT IS ONE GUY WITH A CALCULATOR, AND HE IS\n955\t    SWEATING.\" · \"REMEMBER, KIDS: STAY IN SCHOOL. AND IN THE PAINT.\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM COLA: NOW WITH 30% MORE FIZZ AND 0%\n956\t    EXPLANATION.\" · \"IF YOU'RE JUST JOINING US: YES, THAT WAS A REAL DUNK. NO, WE DON'T KNOW HOW EITHER.\" · \"WE ASKED THE\n957\t    ROBOTS FOR A HALFTIME COMMENT. THEY SENT US A RECEIPT.\"\n958\t15. **sponsor breaks** (one per shatter) — \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK AFTER THIS MESSAGE FROM GLOBO-BLAM GLASS: NOW 40% LESS\n959\t    SHATTERY!\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM INSURANCE: BECAUSE SOMEBODY HAS TO PAY FOR THAT.\" · \"THIS REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD IS BROUGHT\n960\t    TO YOU BY... THE LAST REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD.\"\n961\t\n962\t### 10.7 Announcer lines (`05-data-lines.js`)\n963\t\n964\tBanks by event, at least 10 lines each (write them in the voice of the samples), ALL CAPS, at most 60 characters a\n965\tline, with `{NAME}`, `{VICTIM}`, `{TEAM}` slots. Rules: big plays interrupt small ones; at most two captions per\n966\tpossession; no line repeats within the last 8; per-bank cooldowns; Settings → Commentary (Full, Big plays, Off). VINNIE\n967\tcalls the play, DEE DEE adds the color; alternate them. Samples:\n968\t\n969\t| Bank | Samples |\n970\t|---|---|\n971\t| tipoff | \"WELCOME TO CHANNEL BLAM! LET'S GET LOUD!\" · \"THE BALL IS UP! THE CROWD IS UP! I AM UP!\" |\n972\t| dunk (power) | \"BLAMMO! {NAME} JUST MAILED IT FIRST CLASS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL A CARPENTER, THAT RIM IS FINISHED!\" · \"KA-BLAM! THE CROWD LEFT THEIR SEATS. AND THEIR SHOES!\" |\n973\t| dunk (spin, flip, hang, long) | \"{NAME} SPUN SO FAST THE SCOREBOARD GOT DIZZY!\" · \"A FRONT FLIP?! THAT'S NOT BASKETBALL, THAT'S THE CIRCUS!\" · \"{NAME} IS HANGING ON THAT RIM LIKE IT OWES MONEY!\" · \"AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL HAS QUESTIONS FOR {NAME}!\" |\n974\t| alley-oop | \"SPECIAL DELIVERY! SIGNED, SEALED, SLAMMED!\" |\n975\t| three / deep three | \"SPLASH! BRING A TOWEL!\" · \"THAT WAS FROM A DIFFERENT ZIP CODE!\" · \"{NAME} SHOT THAT FROM THE PARKING LOT! VALIDATED!\" |\n976\t| airball | \"AIRBALL! THE SEAGULLS SAY THANK YOU!\" · \"THAT ONE IS STILL GOING. IT'S IN ORBIT.\" |\n977\t| block | \"REJECTED! RETURN TO SENDER!\" · \"{NAME} SAYS NOT IN MY HOUSE, NOT IN MY YARD, NOT IN MY ZIP CODE!\" |\n978\t| steal | \"PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!\" · \"{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!\" |\n979\t| shove | \"NO FOULS IN BASKETBLAM, BABY!\" · \"THAT'S NOT A FOUL. THAT'S A LIFESTYLE.\" · \"{VICTIM} JUST GOT SENT TO THE SHADOW REALM!\" |\n980\t| ankles | \"ANKLES! {VICTIM} NEEDS A NEW PAIR!\" |\n981\t| posterized | \"FRAME IT! HANG IT! {VICTIM} IS ON {NAME}'S WALL NOW!\" |\n982\t| Supernova on / off | \"{NAME} HAS GONE SUPERNOVA! DIM THE LIGHTS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL NASA, {NAME} IS A STAR!\" · \"AND THE STAR COLLAPSES! BACK TO EARTH, {NAME}!\" |\n983\t| shatter | \"THE GLASS! THE GLASS IS GONE!\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A BROOM. A BIGGER BROOM!\" |\n984\t| goaltend | \"GOALTENDING! THE BUCKET COUNTS, AND SO DOES THE SHAME!\" |\n985\t| jackpot | \"JACKPOT! {NAME} HIT THE SPOT AND THE SPOT PAID OUT!\" |\n986\t| power-ups | \"ROCKET KICKS! {NAME} IS LEGALLY A VEHICLE NOW!\" · \"GLUE GLOVES! THAT BALL ISN'T GOING ANYWHERE!\" · \"LASER SIGHT! {NAME} CAN SEE THE FUTURE, AND IT'S A BUCKET!\" · \"MOON SHOES! GRAVITY HAS LEFT THE BUILDING!\" · \"BLAM BOMB! EVERYBODY DUCK!\" · \"GOLD BALL! NEXT BUCKET'S WORTH DOUBLE!\" |\n987\t| clutch / buzzer | \"TEN SECONDS! HEARTS POUNDING! SNEAKERS SQUEAKING!\" · \"AT THE BUZZER! I BROKE MY CHAIR! I NEED A NEW CHAIR!\" |\n988\t| comeback / blowout | \"{TEAM} IS CLAWING BACK! DON'T TOUCH THAT DIAL!\" · \"THIS ONE'S GETTING UGLY. I'M COVERING MY EYES. I'M PEEKING.\" |\n989\t| twists | \"BIG GUST OFF THE OCEAN! HOLD ONTO YOUR HATS AND YOUR JUMPERS!\" · \"{NAME} HIT THE OIL! THAT'S A SLIP 'N SLAM!\" · \"THE VOLCANO WANTS IN ON THE ACTION!\" · \"{NAME} RODE THE STEAM VENT TO THE MOON!\" |\n990\t| boss | \"THE ROBOTS ARE OVERCLOCKING! SMELLS LIKE BURNT TOAST IN HERE!\" · \"SYSTEM REBOOT! TURN IT OFF AND ON AGAIN, BABY!\" · \"THOSE ROBOTS RUN ON BATTERIES AND BAD MANNERS!\" |\n991\t| shot clock | \"SHOT CLOCK! YOU HAVE TO SHOOT IT EVENTUALLY, FOLKS!\" |\n992\t| quarter end / halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE QUARTER! CATCH YOUR BREATH, I CAN'T!\" · \"HALFTIME! STRETCH YOUR LEGS AND YOUR VOCABULARY!\" · \"FINAL! {TEAM} TAKES IT!\" |\n993\t\n994\tPlayers also bark short trash talk when they taunt, dunk on someone or get a steal (3–5 lines each in their own voice,\n995\te.g. VOLT \"Too slow!\", BIG RUMBLE \"Move.\", SPARKPLUG \"Mine now!\", DUNKATRON \"BALL. ACQUIRED.\").\n996\t\n997\t### 10.8 Cheat codes and unlocks\n998\t\n999\tEntered on the matchup card by any player (`input.sequence(steps, { window: .6 })`); each gives a chime and a line\n1000\t(\"BIG HEADS: ON\"); they last for that game.\n1001\t\n1002\t| Code | Steps | Effect |\n1003\t|---|---|---|\n1004\t| BIG HEADS | up, up, turbo, pass | heads × 1.9 |\n1005\t| POWER-UPS ON | shoot, shoot, pass, turbo | power-ups on this game |\n1006\t| INFINITE TURBO | turbo, turbo, turbo, up, up | infinite turbo for the entering player's side |\n1007\t| NO TWISTS | down, down, shove | the court's twist off |\n1008\t| SKY DUNKS | oop, oop, up, shoot | dunk range from half court |\n1009\t| MOON GRAVITY | up, oop, up, oop | gravity × .55 for players and the ball |\n1010\t| TOURNAMENT MODE | down, left, right, down | no power-ups, twists, comeback assist or other codes: a \"pure\" game |\n1011\t\n1012\tAny code but TOURNAMENT MODE marks the game ★ (no Hall of Blam). Finishing the Tour unlocks the BLAMBOTS and the\n1013\tALL-STARS in Exhibition, the Big heads setting, and the About screen's SECRETS page (which lists the codes). Dev mode\n1014\tcan unlock everything.\n1015\t\n1016\t### 10.9 Blam Camp (`44-camp.js`)\n1017\t\n1018\tOn your team's home court (the Skybox if none chosen). DEE DEE coaches through captions and voice; INTERN 1 and 2 are\n1019\tthe practice partners (scripted or passive CPU). Each lesson: an instruction card with glyph prompts (`promptLine`), a\n1020\tgoal counter, \"NICE!\" on success, then the next. Lessons can be picked from a list and skipped; completion is saved.\n1021\t\n1022\t1. **MOVE & TURBO** — run through three cones; cross the court in under 4 s with turbo.\n1023\t2. **PASS** — pass to your teammate twice; then press pass while the teammate holds it (\"call for it\").\n1024\t3. **JUMP SHOT** — make two jumpers from the marked spots, one of them PERFECT.\n1025\t4. **THREE** — make a three from beyond the arc.\n1026\t5. **DUNK** — hold turbo, drive and press shoot inside the dunk ring on the floor: two dunks.\n1027\t6. **ALLEY-OOP** — press oop to lob to your cutting teammate; then cut and press oop to call for one.\n1028\t7. **STEAL & SPIN** — strip an intern (from the side works best); beat an intern with a spin move.\n1029\t8. **BLOCK & SHOVE** — block an intern's jumper; shove an intern (it's legal!).\n1030\t9. **REBOUND** — grab an intern's miss; then a putback dunk.\n1031\t10. **SUPERNOVA & THE RULES** — score three in a row against passive interns: SUPERNOVA; then the rules card: no\n1032\t    fouls; goaltending counts for the shooter; 20-second shot clock; dunks need turbo; nobody leaves the court; three\n1033\t    straight = SUPERNOVA. \"YOU'RE READY!\"\n1034\t\n1035\t---\n1036\t\n1037\t## 11. Modes, screens and UX\n1038\t\n1039\t### 11.1 The 10-foot rules\n1040\t\n1041\t- Body text is the 5×7 font at scale 1 or more (about 32 px tall at 1080p); headings scale 2–3; titles 4–6. Never the\n1042\t  3×5 `tiny` font for anything a player needs.\n1043\t- At most six focusable items in a group; one obvious primary action; the focus is an animated 2-px outline, a ▸, a\n1044\t  gentle pulse and a brighter fill (never color alone). Title-safe margins of 5% on every side.\n1045\t- A prompt bar at the bottom of every menu screen, in the last-used device's glyphs (\"✕ SELECT  ○ BACK\").\n1046\t- Mouse: hovering a focusable item moves the focus to it; left click activates; right click goes back; the wheel\n1047\t  scrolls lists and turns a slider under the pointer. Keyboard: arrows or WASD move, Enter or Space activate, Esc or\n1048\t  Backspace go back, Q/E or Tab switch tabs. Pad: d-pad or stick move (with repeat), ✕ selects, ○ goes back, L1/R1\n1049\t  switch tabs, Options opens Settings on menu screens. Every screen works with any one device alone.\n1050\t- Teams are told apart by names and positions as well as colors; human players carry P1–P4 tags.\n1051\t\n1052\t### 11.2 Prompts and glyphs (`40-ui-kit.js`)\n1053\t\n1054\t- `glyphIcon(action, player)` follows the player's `lastDevice`: on a gamepad, `input.label(action, 'gamepad')` with\n1055\t  `input.glyphs` set to `'playstation'` (default) or `'xbox'`, mapped to icon sprites; on the keyboard a keycap with\n1056\t  `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`'s text; after mouse use, a mouse icon with the bound button lit (for actions with a\n1057\t  mouse binding; else the keycap).\n1058\t- Icons are drawn once at boot into sprites at 9 px (prompt lines) and 16 px (How to Play): PlayStation ✕ (blue X on a\n1059\t  dark disc), ○ (red ring), □ (pink square), △ (green triangle), L1 R1 L2 R2, OPTIONS, CREATE, d-pad, sticks; Xbox A\n1060\t  (green), B (red), X (blue), Y (yellow), LB RB LT RT, Menu, View; keycaps sized to their text; a mouse with the left or\n1061\t  right half lit.\n1062\t- `promptLine(g, 'Hold {turbo} + {shoot} to DUNK', x, y, { player })` swaps `{action}` tokens for icons (`{move}` shows\n1063\t  the stick or WASD).\n1064\t- Settings → Button symbols (PlayStation | Xbox) sets `glyphs` on every player's input, including players who join\n1065\t  later. The pixel font has no ✕○□△, so canvas prompts always use the icons; the engine's HTML screens show its own text.\n1066\t\n1067\t### 11.3 Screen flow\n1068\t\n1069\t```\n1070\tBOOT → TITLE (\"PRESS START\") ──(10 s without input)──> ATTRACT ──(any input)──> back where it started\n1071\tTITLE → MAIN MENU: BLAM TOUR · EXHIBITION · BLAM CAMP · HALL OF BLAM · HOW TO PLAY · OPTIONS · ABOUT\n1072\t  BLAM TOUR  → CONTINUE TOUR | NEW TOUR → TEAM SELECT (your side) → LINEUP → [PROLOGUE] → TOUR MAP → stops…\n1073\t  EXHIBITION → JOIN (1–4 players, sides) → TEAM SELECT → LINEUP → COURT & RULES → MATCHUP CARD → MATCH → RESULTS\n1074\t  BLAM CAMP  → LESSONS → lesson…        HALL OF BLAM → tables        HOW TO PLAY → 3 pages\n1075\t  OPTIONS    → the engine's Settings (game.menu('settings'))           ABOUT → pages\n1076\tMATCH: TIP-OFF → Q1 → break → Q2 → HALFTIME REPORT → Q3 → break → Q4 → [OT…] → FINAL → RESULTS\n1077\tHub session: OWN CARD → MATCH (2 halves) → RESULTS overlay (the hub ends the round)\n1078\t```\n1079\t\n1080\tTen seconds without input on the title, the main menu or any pre-game menu screen starts the attract mode. Never show a\n1081\tmenu entry for something not built yet: entries arrive with their features.\n1082\t\n1083\t### 11.4 Screens\n1084\t\n1085\t- **Title:** the BASKETBLAM logo (`E.font.title` scale 5–6, \"BLAM\" bursting out of a comic star), the tagline, a\n1086\t  blinking PRESS START with its glyph, the Skybox at night behind it with two players looping an alley-oop, the version\n1087\t  (`E.versionLabel()` and the game's) small at the bottom. Keep the top right (110 × 60 CSS px) clear for the engine's\n1088\t  corner buttons.\n1089\t- **Main menu:** a big list on the left; a live preview panel on the right per entry (the tour map in miniature, two\n1090\t  teams squaring off, a coach's whistle...).\n1091\t- **Join:** four controller slots (P1–P4) in a centre column; each joined player slides its card to HOME (left) or AWAY\n1092\t  (right) with left/right and presses ✕ to be ready, ○ to leave; Start or ✕ on a free pad joins, Enter joins the\n1093\t  keyboard's left half and the engine's key (2) its right half (show which keys each half has). CPU fills empty seats.\n1094\t- **Team select:** two big team cards: logo, name, home court, three player portraits with their eight pip ratings\n1095\t  (icons), a CPU or P badge; left/right cycles, ✕ locks, △ shows the team's bio card.\n1096\t- **Lineup:** three player cards per team; each human picks theirs; the other starter is the best remaining juice.\n1097\t- **Court & rules** (Exhibition): five court cards (locked ones dim) with a preview; quarter length, CPU difficulty,\n1098\t  power-ups, twist; START.\n1099\t- **Matchup card** (\"TONIGHT'S MATCHUP\"): the starters' portraits facing off, ratings, the court; 6 s (each code step in\n1100\t  progress adds 2 s); the cheat-code window; ✕ skips.\n1101\t- **Break card and Halftime Report:** score, quarter leaders, a gag (halftime), juice bars and SUB buttons for human\n1102\t  teams; continues by itself after 8 s (halftime 12 s) unless someone opens subs.\n1103\t- **Results:** FINAL score huge; MVP portrait and a line; BLAM OF THE GAME (the best style play); page 2 a box score (4\n1104\t  rows × PTS REB AST STL BLK DNK); Continue (Tour) / Rematch / New Teams / Main Menu.\n1105\t- **Tour map:** a painted map: Neon Heights' skyline, the Pier on the coast, the Scrapyard inland, Kaboom Island off\n1106\t  shore, the Blam Dome on a hill; a dotted route; stop medallions (won: a W stamp and the score; next: pulsing; later:\n1107\t  dim) that the mouse can hover and click; a side panel with the tour score, the record and the next opponent.\n1108\t- **Hall of Blam:** top-10 tour scores (initials, team, score), and records: most points in a game, best dunk, tours won.\n1109\t- **How to Play:** page 1 a big controller (or keyboard) diagram with a callout per action, following the last device;\n1110\t  page 2 the rules (\"what you can and can't do\", §6.3) and Supernova; page 3 the courts' twists and the power-ups.\n1111\t- **About/Credits:** pages with one topic each (←/→ or L1/R1): CREDITS, SOURCE INFORMATION, TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE\n1112\t  FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK, ENGINE CHANGES, SECRETS (after the Tour). Large text (§16).\n1113\t\n1114\t### 11.5 The match HUD\n1115\t\n1116\t- **Top strip** (y 4–38): HOME panel at the left, AWAY at the right (`E.ui.box`, alpha .85, team colors), each with the\n1117\t  team name, the score (scale 2) and two player plates: name, a 3-px turbo bar, three heat pips, the power-up icon and\n1118\t  countdown, a P badge in the player's color for humans. Panel width = clamp((r.W − 84) / 2 − 8, 116, 170).\n1119\t- **Centre top:** the period (Q1–Q4, OT, SUDDEN BLAM), the game clock (scale 2), the shot clock in a box under it (red\n1120\t  under 5 s, a beep each second from 3).\n1121\t- **In the world:** a P1–P4 arrow tag over each human's player; a turbo ring under a player holding turbo; a soft ring\n1122\t  under the ball handler; edge arrows for humans off screen; the release meter by the shooter and the dunk-range ring\n1123\t  under a human handler holding turbo (Settings → Shot meter).\n1124\t- **Bottom centre:** the announcer's lower-third caption (portrait, name, two lines, non-modal). It is our own widget,\n1125\t  not an `E.Dialog`, so shoot and pass (which double as the engine's confirm) never skip it; `E.Dialog` is for story\n1126\t  beats only. Bottom left at the Pier: the windsock.\n1127\t\n1128\t### 11.6 Pause menu and settings\n1129\t\n1130\t- The engine's standard pause menu (an HTML Shell), themed: `new E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#fff7ec', paper:\n1131\t  '#140c24', accent: '#ff3ca6', muted: '#9a8fb8', danger: '#ff5a3a', line: '#3a2a5a', font: '700 1rem/1.35 \"Trebuchet\n1132\t  MS\", system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: '900 1.6rem/1 Impact, \"Arial Black\", system-ui' }, screens: { help:\n1133\t  HOW_TO_PLAY_HELP } })`, plus a CSS rule so its text scales for a TV (`.esh { font-size: clamp(18px, 2.6vh, 42px) }`);\n1134\t  check it in a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n1135\t- Pause items: Resume, How to Play, Restart Game (matches), Skip Cutscene (story), **Dev Mode**, then the standard\n1136\t  Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n1137\t- Game settings (group Game, through `menu.settings`): Button symbols (PlayStation | Xbox), CPU difficulty (Rookie | Pro\n1138\t  | All-Star | BLAM; Pro), Quarter length (1:00 | 1:30 | 2:00 | 3:00; 2:00), Power-ups (On | Off), Court twists (On |\n1139\t  Off), Jackpot Spot on every court (Off | On), Comeback assist (Off | Low | Normal), Commentary (Full | Big plays | Off),\n1140\t  Voice volume (slider), Camera (Broadcast | High), Shot meter (On | Off), Big heads (Off | On; defined once unlocked).\n1141\t  The standard ones stay (volume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, pixel scaling, filter, frame rate).\n1142\t\n1143\t### 11.7 Touch-only devices\n1144\t\n1145\t- Touch-only = `navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` and neither `(any-pointer: fine)` nor `(any-hover: hover)` matches, and no\n1146\t  gamepad and no key press seen yet. A `gamepadconnected` event or a first key press switches to normal play at once.\n1147\t- While touch-only: no touch controls at all (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, every scene `touch: []`); the title\n1148\t  shows **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** (scale 2, centred) and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n1149\t  `game.menu('settings')`); nothing else answers taps; after 10 s the attract mode runs as usual and keeps looping, and\n1150\t  a tap during it shows the notice and the button over it for 4 s instead of leaving.\n1151\t\n1152\t---\n1153\t\n1154\t## 12. Audio (every sound, song and voice made in code)\n1155\t\n1156\t### 12.1 Music\n1157\t\n1158\tEngine songs (`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, notes, on }] }`; Appendix C has a complete one), layers\n1159\tswitched with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`, jingles with `audio.sting`.\n1160\t\n1161\t| Song | Where | Feel | bpm | Key | Layers |\n1162\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1163\t| `title` | title, main menu | funk anthem: slap bass, saw brass stabs, boom-bap | 108 | E minor | `hype` lead after 8 bars |\n1164\t| `menu` | pre-game menus | the anthem's bass and drums | 108 | E minor | – |\n1165\t| `skybox` | the Skybox | electro-funk, arpeggios | 116 | A minor | `nova` |\n1166\t| `pier` | the Pier | surf-funk, twangy pulse lead | 124 | D major | `nova` |\n1167\t| `scrapyard` | the Scrapyard | industrial boom-bap, metallic noise hits | 92 | C minor | `nova` |\n1168\t| `caldera` | the Caldera | tiki drums and bass, marimba-like triangle | 128 | G minor pentatonic | `nova` |\n1169\t| `dome` | the Blam Dome | arena rock-hop, saw power chords, big drums | 132 | E minor | `nova`, `overclock` (frantic arpeggio), `clutch` (more drums) |\n1170\t| `halftime` | halftime report | chip marching band | 120 | B♭ major | – |\n1171\t| `tourmap` | tour map | travel groove | 100 | F major | – |\n1172\t| `story` | cutscenes | tension bed: drones, sparse plucks | 84 | D minor | `villain` (organ) |\n1173\t| `camp` | Blam Camp | light practice loop | 104 | C major | – |\n1174\t| `credits` | ending, credits | the anthem in a major key | 112 | E major | – |\n1175\t\n1176\tStings: `tip`, `buzzer`, `nova`, `shatter`, `victory`, `defeat`, `unlock`, `sponsor` (a 4-s cheesy ad jingle). Dynamics:\n1177\tthe last 30 s of Q4 or overtime within 6 points bring in `clutch` and `audio.tempo(bpm + 6)`; Supernova brings `nova`;\n1178\tOverclock brings `overclock`; music dips 25% while a voice speaks. Tracks of different loop lengths phase against each\n1179\tother (the engine loops each on its own length); melody vol ≤ .08, bass ≤ .3, drums about .1.\n1180\t\n1181\t### 12.2 Sound effects\n1182\t\n1183\tDefined with `audio.define(name, voice)` (the engine's voices: `{ wave, freq, to, dur, vol, filter, vib, arp, step }`\n1184\tor a list of them); played through one policy function that sets volume by distance from the camera's centre.\n1185\t\n1186\t| Group | Sounds |\n1187\t|---|---|\n1188\t| ball | `dribble_asphalt`, `dribble_planks`, `dribble_concrete`, `dribble_stone`, `dribble_maple` (a sine thump 140 → 60 Hz, .07 s, plus a material tick of noise), `bounce`, `catch` (a soft slap), `release` (a short noise whoosh) |\n1189\t| hoop | `swish` (noise swept up 2 → 6 kHz, .25 s), `rim` (square 620 Hz + triangle 1240 Hz, fast decay, a click), `backboard` (triangle 160 → 110 Hz + a thud), `net_snap`, `slam` (sine 80 → 40 Hz boom + rim + crowd), `shatter` (a .5-s noise burst + 20 random high sine pings 2–6 kHz over .6 s) |\n1190\t| players | `squeak` (sine 2600 → 3400 Hz, .09 s, vibrato), `step`, `jump`, `land_heavy`, `turbo_loop` (low-pass noise while held), `shove` (punch + whoosh), `fall` (thump and rattle), `steal` (swipe + pop), `block` (slap + boom), `spin` (whoosh), `dizzy` (little tweets) |\n1191\t| match | `whistle`, `buzzer` (square 220 + 230 Hz beating, .9 s), `shotclock_beep`, `horn` (overtime), `crowd_roar`, `crowd_ooh`, `crowd_boo`, `camera_flash` (tiny clicks) |\n1192\t| power-ups and twists | `pu_spawn` (pulse arpeggio 0-4-7-12), `pu_pick` (the engine's `powerup`), `pu_end`, `jackpot`, `nova_on` (saw sweep 200 → 1600 Hz + crackle), `wind_gust` (band-passed noise sweep), `gull`, `oil_slip`, `rumble` (low noise 80–200 Hz, 1.5 s), `bomb_whistle` (sine 1200 → 400 Hz), `bomb_hit` (the engine's `explode`), `vent_puff`, `pyro`, `servo` (saw 300 → 500 Hz, vibrato), `reboot` (descending glitchy square) |\n1193\t| UI | the engine's `select`, `confirm`, `cancel`, `pause`; `code_ok` (a chime), `stamp` (the tour map's W stamp) |\n1194\t\n1195\t### 12.3 Voices: Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish (`12-audio-voice.js`)\n1196\t\n1197\t- `Voice.say(text, profile, { onEnd })` speaks a caption; `Voice.letter(ch, profile)` speaks while a Dialog types\n1198\t  (engine change 3). Text becomes syllables (a consonant cluster plus a vowel; digits and symbols skipped; spaces are\n1199\t  short gaps; punctuation longer ones)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad0c147-1299-4fc9-adba-2f06893c3033","uuid":"86d4888d-33bf-40c3-83bd-d4f95584821e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:09:12.128Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/PLAN.md","content":"the player answers the Overclock. Pyro columns fire on every score (cosmetic, with light flashes).\n\n### 10.2 Teams and players\n\nRatings in the order ZOOM / SPLASH / DEEP / SLAM / DIME / SWIPE / SWAT / BUMP.\n\n| Team | Colors (jersey / trim / shorts) | Logo | Style |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS | `#ff3ca6` / `#2de2ff` / `#1a1420` | a winged sneaker | flashy, fast, high-flying |\n| BOARDWALK BREAKERS | `#18c8b8` / `#ff7a5c` / `#f2d8a0` | a breaking wave | passing and threes |\n| SCRAPYARD CRUSHERS | `#d8641e` / `#ffd23a` / `#1c1a18` | crossed wrenches | power and steals |\n| KABOOM MAGMA | `#ff3a1a` / `#ffb020` / `#22181e` | a volcano erupting a basketball | defense and clutch shooting |\n| THE BLAMBOTS (boss; unlocked by the Tour) | `#c8d0dc` / `#e8c040` / `#3a4250` | a robot fist holding a ball | everything, loudly |\n| CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS (secret; unlocked by the Tour) | `#f4f0ea` / `#ffc83a` / `#4a2a8a` | the Channel BLAM microphone | showbiz |\n\n| Player | Team | Role | Build, size | Look | Ratings | Voice | Taunt |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VOLT | Hightops | high-flyer | heroic 1.65 | electric-blue ponytail, magenta band, skin `#8a5a3c` | 9 5 4 9 6 6 4 3 | bright, quick, 220 Hz | raise the roof |\n| BIG RUMBLE | Hightops | enforcer | bulky 1.9 | black flattop, cyan wristbands, skin `#4a2c1e` | 3 3 1 7 4 4 9 10 | deep, slow, 85 Hz | flex |\n| PIXEL | Hightops | sharpshooter | heroic 1.55 | green spiky hair, shades, skin `#f0c8a0` | 6 9 9 3 7 5 3 3 | squeaky, 270 Hz | finger guns |\n| RIPTIDE | Breakers | point guard | heroic 1.6 | long sun-bleached hair, skin `#d8a070` | 10 6 6 5 10 7 2 3 | laid-back drawl, 170 Hz | surf balance |\n| SHELLSHOCK | Breakers | three-point bomber | heroic 1.65 | coral afro, skin `#6a4028` | 6 8 10 3 6 5 3 4 | sing-song, 200 Hz | goggles (hands circle the eyes) |\n| LONGBOARD | Breakers | shot blocker | heroic 1.85, legs × 1.12 | bald, teal band, skin `#c89070` | 4 5 2 7 4 3 9 7 | slow, 120 Hz | finger wag |\n| TORQUE | Crushers | power dunker | bulky 1.85 | black mohawk, skin `#c8a080` | 6 4 2 10 4 4 6 9 | gravel, 95 Hz (noise in it) | chest pound |\n| SPARKPLUG | Crushers | pickpocket | chibi 1.65 | yellow cap, skin `#3a2418` | 9 6 6 4 7 10 2 2 | fast, 300 Hz | shimmy |\n| HUBCAP | Crushers | veteran all-rounder | heroic 1.7 | short grey hair, skin `#e0b090` | 5 7 6 6 6 6 6 6 | grumpy, 130 Hz | taps an imaginary watch |\n| OBSIDIAN | Magma | rim protector | bulky 1.95 | bald, skin `#3a2216` | 4 4 1 8 3 4 10 8 | rumbling, 78 Hz | arms crossed, stone face |\n| EMBER | Magma | clutch shooter | heroic 1.6 | long red hair, skin `#f0c090` | 7 9 8 5 6 6 3 3 | crisp, 230 Hz | blows on fingertips |\n| PUMICE | Magma | leaper | heroic 1.65 | black afro, skin `#8a5030` | 8 5 3 9 5 5 7 3 | bouncy, 190 Hz | pogo hops |\n| DUNKATRON | Blambots | destroyer | bulky 1.95, chrome helmet, red eye glow | chrome body, gold trim | 8 6 4 10 6 8 8 8 | robot, 95 Hz | robot dance |\n| SWATBOT | Blambots | wall | bulky 1.95, same | chrome, red visor | 6 7 7 7 7 9 10 9 | robot, 120 Hz | \"processing\" head tilt |\n| SPARE PARTS | Blambots | bench unit | bulky 1.8, same | mismatched panels | 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 | glitchy robot, 150 Hz | glitch wave |\n| VINNIE VOX | All-Stars | play-by-play man | heroic 1.7 | headset band, skin `#e8b890` | 5 7 7 5 8 5 4 5 | the announcer (low) | mic drop |\n| DEE DEE DECIBEL | All-Stars | color commentator | heroic 1.6 | purple ponytail, skin `#6a4030` | 7 8 6 6 7 6 5 4 | the announcer (high) | points at the camera |\n| BLAMMO | All-Stars | the league's gorilla mascot | bulky 2.0, hunch .2 | dark fur (skin and hair `#3a2e2a`), lighter face | 7 3 1 10 3 6 9 10 | gorilla | chest drum |\n\nStory characters (not playable): **COMMISSIONER GIGAWATT** (CEO of GLOBO-BLAM Corp; heroic 1.6, purple coat, gold belt,\nwhite hair, a smug smile; a nasal, slow voice), **REF ROSCOE** (referee; white shirt with black trim, black cap, a\nwhistle; tosses the tip-off), **INTERN 1 and INTERN 2** (Blam Camp partners in grey practice jerseys), the **cleaning\nbot** (a small metal Blob that replaces shattered glass). Vinnie and Dee Dee also appear at the studio desk in suits\n(`outfit: 'coat'`). Every line about a player uses the player's NAME, never a pronoun, so any line fits any player.\n\n### 10.3 Dunk catalog (`06-data-moves.js`)\n\n| Id | Banner | Needs | Distance from rim | Choreography (u = flight progress) | Style bonus |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `hammer` | TWO-HAND HAMMER | any | 0–70 | both hands raise the ball overhead from takeoff; slam at u .9 | 0 |\n| `tomahawk` | TOMAHAWK! | SLAM 5 | 30–130 | ball in the right hand cocked far behind the head (u .3–.7), whipped forward at .88 | 50 |\n| `doublepump` | DOUBLE PUMP! | SLAM 6 | 30–120 | ball pumped to the waist and back up twice (u .3, .55) | 80 |\n| `reverse` | REVERSE ROCKET! | SLAM 6, approach within 50° of the baseline | 20–100 | turns its back to the rim mid-flight, slams backward over the head | 100 |\n| `windmill` | WINDMILL! | SLAM 7 | 50–150 | right arm circles once (down past the hip, back, over the top) | 100 |\n| `threesixty` | THREE-SIXTY! | SLAM 7 | 40–140 | facing turns 2π over u .2–.85; two-hand slam | 120 |\n| `ftflyer` | FREE-THROW FLYER! | SLAM 8 | 110 to the dunk range | a long glide (apex + 30), legs split, one-hand slam | 150 |\n| `flip` | FRONT-FLIP FREAK! | SLAM 8 | 60–150 | `flip` 0 → 1 over u .25–.75 (a front somersault), two-hand slam | 180 |\n| `rattler` | RIM RATTLER! | SLAM 4 | 0–60 | two-hand slam, then `hang` 1.2 s with legs swinging | 60 |\n| `nova720` | SEVEN-TWENTY SUPERNOVA! | Supernova | 60–190 | facing turns 4π, star-fire trail | 250 |\n| `volcano` | VOLCANO LAUNCH! | a steam vent | from the vent | launched (apex 160), a 2π spin, a fireball slam; shatters 20% | 300 |\n| `quake` | BLAM-QUAKE!!! | overclocked BLAMBOT; Moon Shoes 50%; Supernova 15% | 80 to the dunk range | huge apex, both hands, always shatters, the landing's shockwave knocks down everyone within 40 | 400 |\n\nChoice: every dunk whose needs pass, weighted by its bonus and by (SLAM − its minimum + 1), drawn with `S.rng`; the\nsame for humans and the CPU. Each has an announcer line family (power, spin, flip, hang, long, nova, volcano, quake).\n\n### 10.4 Power-up icons\n\n12×12 string sprites, drawn bobbing above a pulsing floor ring in their color: ROCKET KICKS (a sneaker with a flame),\nGLUE GLOVES (a green dripping glove), LASER SIGHT (a red crosshair), MOON SHOES (a spring shoe), BLAM BOMB (a black bomb\nwith a lit fuse), GOLD BALL (a gold ball with a shine). The same icons show on the players' plates with a countdown.\n\n### 10.5 The Blam Tour\n\nPROLOGUE → STOP 1 → STOP 2 → STOP 3 → THE REVEAL → THE FINAL → ENDING → CREDITS → HALL OF BLAM ENTRY.\n\n| You pick | Stop 1 | Stop 2 | Stop 3 | Final |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hightops | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Breakers | Hightops at the Skybox | Crushers at the Scrapyard | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Crushers | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Magma at the Caldera | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n| Magma | Hightops at the Skybox | Breakers at the Pier | Crushers at the Scrapyard | BLAMBOTS at the Blam Dome |\n\n- CPU difficulty: the Settings value (default Pro) shifted by stop: stop 1 one step lower, stop 2 as set, stop 3 half a\n  step higher, the final one step higher (clamped to BLAM).\n- Power-ups off at stop 1, on from stop 2. Quarters 1:30. One or two players (a second human joins on the same team at\n  the Tour's team select).\n- Each stop: tour map → matchup card (codes) → pre-game talk → tip-off → the game → results → post-game beat → map\n  (autosave). A loss: results → REMATCH? 10-second countdown (Rematch, Tour Map, Quit Tour); a rematch replays the stop.\n- Tour score = the stops' style points (wins only). At the end, or on quitting after a loss, a qualifying score enters\n  the Hall of Blam (`E.Arcade` initials wheel).\n\n### 10.6 Story script (`04-data-story.js`)\n\nTone: a loud 90s sports broadcast. Announcers speak in ALL CAPS, punchy, pun-heavy; the Commissioner is smug and speaks\nin sentence case; robots speak in SPACED. CAPITAL. WORDS. `{TEAM}` is your team's name; `{CAPTAIN}` your first player.\nBeats play in engine scenes (§11.3) as `E.Dialog` lines with live portraits and voices, staged with posed rigs and camera\nmoves (`game.script`, `game.tween`). Hold confirm 1 s to skip a beat, Start to skip all of it.\n\n1. **prologue** (the Channel BLAM studio desk; the Commissioner on a monitor)\n   - VINNIE: \"GOOD EVENING, BALL FANS! LIVE FROM THE TOP OF THE WORLD, THIS IS CHANNEL BLAM!\"\n   - DEE DEE: \"AND THIS IS THE BLAM TOUR! FIVE COURTS! FOUR CREWS! ONE GOLDEN BLAMBOOZLE! ZERO FOULS!\"\n   - VINNIE: \"TONIGHT'S TOUR IS SPONSORED BY GLOBO-BLAM CORP. THEY MAKE EVERYTHING. THEY MADE THIS SENTENCE.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Greetings, little ballers. Win my Tour and the Golden Blamboozle is yours.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Lose, and your court becomes a GLOBO-BLAM parking lot. Validated parking, of course. Ha. Ha. Ha.\"\n   - DEE DEE: \"{TEAM}, THE WHOLE CITY IS WATCHING. NO PRESSURE! EXCEPT ALL OF IT!\"\n2. **camp-offer** (first Tour only) — DEE DEE: \"FIRST TIME ON THE TOUR? HIT BLAM CAMP AND I'LL SHOW YOU THE ROPES. OR\n   DON'T. LIVE DANGEROUSLY!\" Choices: BLAM CAMP / LET'S PLAY.\n3. **stop intro** (each stop, at the court) — VINNIE: \"STOP {N} OF THE BLAM TOUR: {HOME} VERSUS {AWAY} AT {COURT}!\" plus\n   DEE DEE's court line: Skybox \"THIRTY STORIES UP AND THE NETS ARE STILL SMOKING!\"; Pier \"WATCH THE WIND, FOLKS. AND THE\n   SEAGULLS. MOSTLY THE SEAGULLS.\"; Scrapyard \"OIL ON THE FLOOR AND FIRE IN THEIR EYES!\"; Caldera \"THE FLOOR IS HOT, THE\n   VOLCANO IS HOTTER, AND THE MUSIC IS HOTTEST!\"; Dome \"THE BLAM DOME! SIXTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE VERY NERVOUS\n   JUMBOTRON!\"\n4. **pre-game talk** (the rival captain, then your captain's reply by team):\n   - vs Breakers — RIPTIDE: \"Hope you packed sunscreen, {TEAM}. The tide's coming in, and it doesn't knock.\" Replies:\n     VOLT \"Cute pier. I'm about to dunk on it.\" · TORQUE \"I've crushed bigger boats than this.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Sand turns\n     to glass when I'm around.\"\n   - vs Hightops — VOLT: \"Welcome to the Skybox. Try not to look down. Actually, look down: that's where you'll be.\"\n     Replies: RIPTIDE \"Whoa, relax. We're just here to ride the wave. Over you.\" · TORQUE \"Fancy lights. They'll look\n     great on my scrap pile.\" · EMBER \"Neon's cute. Lava's hotter.\"\n   - vs Crushers — TORQUE: \"We crush cars for breakfast. You look like a light snack.\" Replies: VOLT \"Then you're about\n     to get a stomachache.\" · SHELLSHOCK \"Careful, the floor's greasier than your jokes.\" · PUMICE \"I bounce. You crush.\n     Let's see who's still standing.\"\n   - vs Magma — OBSIDIAN: \"On Kaboom Island the floor is lava. Not a game. Actual lava. Walk carefully.\" Replies:\n     BIG RUMBLE \"I don't walk carefully. I walk LOUD.\" · RIPTIDE \"Dude. Is that, like, safe?\" · SPARKPLUG \"I'm too fast\n     to get burned!\"\n5. **post-game, stop 1** — the beaten captain: RIPTIDE \"Wipeout. Totally gnarly, though. Respect.\" · VOLT \"Okay, okay.\n   You can ball. Don't let it go to your head.\" · TORQUE \"You crushed us. That's MY job.\" · OBSIDIAN \"The mountain...\n   respects you.\" Then GIGAWATT (monitor): \"Hmm. Promising. My engineers are taking notes. Lots of notes.\"\n6. **post-game, stop 2** — GIGAWATT: \"Data received. Prototype calibration at ninety-eight percent. Keep playing,\n   little ballers. Keep... teaching them.\" DEE DEE: \"TEACHING WHO? VINNIE, WHY DOES THE GLOBO-BLAM LOGO HAVE A ROBOT\n   ARM?\" VINNIE: \"THAT'S BRANDING, DEE DEE. WE DON'T ASK QUESTIONS ON LIVE TV.\"\n7. **the reveal** (after stop 3, at the Dome, the Commissioner in person)\n   - VINNIE: \"THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Congratulations. You have earned the privilege... of being replaced.\"\n   - GIGAWATT: \"Behold the future of basketball: the BLAMBOTS! No salaries! No sweat! No mercy!\"\n   - DUNKATRON: \"BEEP. YOUR. CAREER. IS. DEPRECATED.\"\n   - SWATBOT: \"INITIATING. TRASH. TALK. PROTOCOL. ... YOU. STINK.\"\n   - {CAPTAIN} by team: VOLT \"Did the toaster just trash-talk me?\" · RIPTIDE \"Bummer. I was gonna say we could be\n     friends.\" · TORQUE \"I've got a crusher with your names on it.\" · OBSIDIAN \"Metal melts.\"\n8. **final pre-game** — VINNIE: \"THE FINAL! HUMANS VERSUS HARDWARE! THE BLAMBOOZLE IS ON THE LINE!\"\n9. **overclock** (in play, captions and the jumbotron) — GIGAWATT: \"OVERCLOCK THEM! MAXIMUM BLAM!\" DEE DEE: \"THE ROBOTS\n   ARE GLOWING! IS THAT LEGAL? THERE ARE NO RULES! I FORGOT!\"\n10. **first reboot** (in play, once) — DEE DEE: \"THEY SHORT-CIRCUIT WHEN YOU KNOCK THEM DOWN! KEEP SHOVING, {TEAM}!\"\n11. **ending** (after winning the final)\n    - DUNKATRON: \"ERROR. ERROR. HUMANS. TOO. ... BLAM.\" (sparks; both bots topple)\n    - VINNIE: \"THEY DID IT! {TEAM} WINS THE BLAM TOUR!\"\n    - DEE DEE: \"AND THE BLAMBOTS ARE BEING RECYCLED INTO VERY SAD TOASTERS!\"\n    - GIGAWATT: \"This isn't over! I'll buy another league! I'll buy the MOON! Hey! Put me down!\" (BLAMMO carries the\n      Commissioner off over a shoulder)\n    - VINNIE: \"STREETBALL IS SAVED! THE BLAMBOOZLE GOES HOME WITH {TEAM}!\"\n    - DEE DEE: \"GOODNIGHT, EVERYBODY! REMEMBER: NO FOULS! NO MERCY!\" VINNIE and DEE DEE: \"ALL BLAM!\"\n12. **credits** — scrolling credits over the trophy lift and a crowd confetti storm, the `credits` song; then unlock\n    cards: \"UNLOCKED: THE BLAMBOTS\", \"UNLOCKED: CHANNEL BLAM ALL-STARS\", \"UNLOCKED: BIG HEADS (OPTIONS)\", \"SECRETS ON\n    THE ABOUT SCREEN\".\n13. **losses** — stops 1–3: GIGAWATT \"Tsk. Another court for my parking empire.\" The final: GIGAWATT \"Resistance is...\n    adorable.\" DUNKATRON \"GAME. OVER. INSERT. COIN.\"\n14. **halftime gags** (one per halftime, no repeats within a Tour): \"THIS HALFTIME IS BROUGHT TO YOU BY GLOBO-BLAM\n    SNEAKER GLUE. STICK THE LANDING. FOREVER.\" · \"OUR STATS DEPARTMENT IS ONE GUY WITH A CALCULATOR, AND HE IS\n    SWEATING.\" · \"REMEMBER, KIDS: STAY IN SCHOOL. AND IN THE PAINT.\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM COLA: NOW WITH 30% MORE FIZZ AND 0%\n    EXPLANATION.\" · \"IF YOU'RE JUST JOINING US: YES, THAT WAS A REAL DUNK. NO, WE DON'T KNOW HOW EITHER.\" · \"WE ASKED THE\n    ROBOTS FOR A HALFTIME COMMENT. THEY SENT US A RECEIPT.\"\n15. **sponsor breaks** (one per shatter) — \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK AFTER THIS MESSAGE FROM GLOBO-BLAM GLASS: NOW 40% LESS\n    SHATTERY!\" · \"GLOBO-BLAM INSURANCE: BECAUSE SOMEBODY HAS TO PAY FOR THAT.\" · \"THIS REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD IS BROUGHT\n    TO YOU BY... THE LAST REPLACEMENT BACKBOARD.\"\n\n### 10.7 Announcer lines (`05-data-lines.js`)\n\nBanks by event, at least 10 lines each (write them in the voice of the samples), ALL CAPS, at most 60 characters a\nline, with `{NAME}`, `{VICTIM}`, `{TEAM}` slots. Rules: big plays interrupt small ones; at most two captions per\npossession; no line repeats within the last 8; per-bank cooldowns; Settings → Commentary (Full, Big plays, Off). VINNIE\ncalls the play, DEE DEE adds the color; alternate them. Samples:\n\n| Bank | Samples |\n|---|---|\n| tipoff | \"WELCOME TO CHANNEL BLAM! LET'S GET LOUD!\" · \"THE BALL IS UP! THE CROWD IS UP! I AM UP!\" |\n| dunk (power) | \"BLAMMO! {NAME} JUST MAILED IT FIRST CLASS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL A CARPENTER, THAT RIM IS FINISHED!\" · \"KA-BLAM! THE CROWD LEFT THEIR SEATS. AND THEIR SHOES!\" |\n| dunk (spin, flip, hang, long) | \"{NAME} SPUN SO FAST THE SCOREBOARD GOT DIZZY!\" · \"A FRONT FLIP?! THAT'S NOT BASKETBALL, THAT'S THE CIRCUS!\" · \"{NAME} IS HANGING ON THAT RIM LIKE IT OWES MONEY!\" · \"AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL HAS QUESTIONS FOR {NAME}!\" |\n| alley-oop | \"SPECIAL DELIVERY! SIGNED, SEALED, SLAMMED!\" |\n| three / deep three | \"SPLASH! BRING A TOWEL!\" · \"THAT WAS FROM A DIFFERENT ZIP CODE!\" · \"{NAME} SHOT THAT FROM THE PARKING LOT! VALIDATED!\" |\n| airball | \"AIRBALL! THE SEAGULLS SAY THANK YOU!\" · \"THAT ONE IS STILL GOING. IT'S IN ORBIT.\" |\n| block | \"REJECTED! RETURN TO SENDER!\" · \"{NAME} SAYS NOT IN MY HOUSE, NOT IN MY YARD, NOT IN MY ZIP CODE!\" |\n| steal | \"PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!\" · \"{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!\" |\n| shove | \"NO FOULS IN BASKETBLAM, BABY!\" · \"THAT'S NOT A FOUL. THAT'S A LIFESTYLE.\" · \"{VICTIM} JUST GOT SENT TO THE SHADOW REALM!\" |\n| ankles | \"ANKLES! {VICTIM} NEEDS A NEW PAIR!\" |\n| posterized | \"FRAME IT! HANG IT! {VICTIM} IS ON {NAME}'S WALL NOW!\" |\n| Supernova on / off | \"{NAME} HAS GONE SUPERNOVA! DIM THE LIGHTS!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL NASA, {NAME} IS A STAR!\" · \"AND THE STAR COLLAPSES! BACK TO EARTH, {NAME}!\" |\n| shatter | \"THE GLASS! THE GLASS IS GONE!\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A BROOM. A BIGGER BROOM!\" |\n| goaltend | \"GOALTENDING! THE BUCKET COUNTS, AND SO DOES THE SHAME!\" |\n| jackpot | \"JACKPOT! {NAME} HIT THE SPOT AND THE SPOT PAID OUT!\" |\n| power-ups | \"ROCKET KICKS! {NAME} IS LEGALLY A VEHICLE NOW!\" · \"GLUE GLOVES! THAT BALL ISN'T GOING ANYWHERE!\" · \"LASER SIGHT! {NAME} CAN SEE THE FUTURE, AND IT'S A BUCKET!\" · \"MOON SHOES! GRAVITY HAS LEFT THE BUILDING!\" · \"BLAM BOMB! EVERYBODY DUCK!\" · \"GOLD BALL! NEXT BUCKET'S WORTH DOUBLE!\" |\n| clutch / buzzer | \"TEN SECONDS! HEARTS POUNDING! SNEAKERS SQUEAKING!\" · \"AT THE BUZZER! I BROKE MY CHAIR! I NEED A NEW CHAIR!\" |\n| comeback / blowout | \"{TEAM} IS CLAWING BACK! DON'T TOUCH THAT DIAL!\" · \"THIS ONE'S GETTING UGLY. I'M COVERING MY EYES. I'M PEEKING.\" |\n| twists | \"BIG GUST OFF THE OCEAN! HOLD ONTO YOUR HATS AND YOUR JUMPERS!\" · \"{NAME} HIT THE OIL! THAT'S A SLIP 'N SLAM!\" · \"THE VOLCANO WANTS IN ON THE ACTION!\" · \"{NAME} RODE THE STEAM VENT TO THE MOON!\" |\n| boss | \"THE ROBOTS ARE OVERCLOCKING! SMELLS LIKE BURNT TOAST IN HERE!\" · \"SYSTEM REBOOT! TURN IT OFF AND ON AGAIN, BABY!\" · \"THOSE ROBOTS RUN ON BATTERIES AND BAD MANNERS!\" |\n| shot clock | \"SHOT CLOCK! YOU HAVE TO SHOOT IT EVENTUALLY, FOLKS!\" |\n| quarter end / halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE QUARTER! CATCH YOUR BREATH, I CAN'T!\" · \"HALFTIME! STRETCH YOUR LEGS AND YOUR VOCABULARY!\" · \"FINAL! {TEAM} TAKES IT!\" |\n\nPlayers also bark short trash talk when they taunt, dunk on someone or get a steal (3–5 lines each in their own voice,\ne.g. VOLT \"Too slow!\", BIG RUMBLE \"Move.\", SPARKPLUG \"Mine now!\", DUNKATRON \"BALL. ACQUIRED.\").\n\n### 10.8 Cheat codes and unlocks\n\nEntered on the matchup card by any player (`input.sequence(steps, { window: .6 })`); each gives a chime and a line\n(\"BIG HEADS: ON\"); they last for that game.\n\n| Code | Steps | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| BIG HEADS | up, up, turbo, pass | heads × 1.9 |\n| POWER-UPS ON | shoot, shoot, pass, turbo | power-ups on this game |\n| INFINITE TURBO | turbo, turbo, turbo, up, up | infinite turbo for the entering player's side |\n| NO TWISTS | down, down, shove | the court's twist off |\n| SKY DUNKS | oop, oop, up, shoot | dunk range from half court |\n| MOON GRAVITY | up, oop, up, oop | gravity × .55 for players and the ball |\n| TOURNAMENT MODE | down, left, right, down | no power-ups, twists, comeback assist or other codes: a \"pure\" game |\n\nAny code but TOURNAMENT MODE marks the game ★ (no Hall of Blam). Finishing the Tour unlocks the BLAMBOTS and the\nALL-STARS in Exhibition, the Big heads setting, and the About screen's SECRETS page (which lists the codes). Dev mode\ncan unlock everything.\n\n### 10.9 Blam Camp (`44-camp.js`)\n\nOn your team's home court (the Skybox if none chosen). DEE DEE coaches through captions and voice; INTERN 1 and 2 are\nthe practice partners (scripted or passive CPU). Each lesson: an instruction card with glyph prompts (`promptLine`), a\ngoal counter, \"NICE!\" on success, then the next. Lessons can be picked from a list and skipped; completion is saved.\n\n1. **MOVE & TURBO** — run through three cones; cross the court in under 4 s with turbo.\n2. **PASS** — pass to your teammate twice; then press pass while the teammate holds it (\"call for it\").\n3. **JUMP SHOT** — make two jumpers from the marked spots, one of them PERFECT.\n4. **THREE** — make a three from beyond the arc.\n5. **DUNK** — hold turbo, drive and press shoot inside the dunk ring on the floor: two dunks.\n6. **ALLEY-OOP** — press oop to lob to your cutting teammate; then cut and press oop to call for one.\n7. **STEAL & SPIN** — strip an intern (from the side works best); beat an intern with a spin move.\n8. **BLOCK & SHOVE** — block an intern's jumper; shove an intern (it's legal!).\n9. **REBOUND** — grab an intern's miss; then a putback dunk.\n10. **SUPERNOVA & THE RULES** — score three in a row against passive interns: SUPERNOVA; then the rules card: no\n    fouls; goaltending counts for the shooter; 20-second shot clock; dunks need turbo; nobody leaves the court; three\n    straight = SUPERNOVA. \"YOU'RE READY!\"\n\n---\n\n## 11. Modes, screens and UX\n\n### 11.1 The 10-foot rules\n\n- Body text is the 5×7 font at scale 1 or more (about 32 px tall at 1080p); headings scale 2–3; titles 4–6. Never the\n  3×5 `tiny` font for anything a player needs.\n- At most six focusable items in a group; one obvious primary action; the focus is an animated 2-px outline, a ▸, a\n  gentle pulse and a brighter fill (never color alone). Title-safe margins of 5% on every side.\n- A prompt bar at the bottom of every menu screen, in the last-used device's glyphs (\"✕ SELECT  ○ BACK\").\n- Mouse: hovering a focusable item moves the focus to it; left click activates; right click goes back; the wheel\n  scrolls lists and turns a slider under the pointer. Keyboard: arrows or WASD move, Enter or Space activate, Esc or\n  Backspace go back, Q/E or Tab switch tabs. Pad: d-pad or stick move (with repeat), ✕ selects, ○ goes back, L1/R1\n  switch tabs, Options opens Settings on menu screens. Every screen works with any one device alone.\n- Teams are told apart by names and positions as well as colors; human players carry P1–P4 tags.\n\n### 11.2 Prompts and glyphs (`40-ui-kit.js`)\n\n- `glyphIcon(action, player)` follows the player's `lastDevice`: on a gamepad, `input.label(action, 'gamepad')` with\n  `input.glyphs` set to `'playstation'` (default) or `'xbox'`, mapped to icon sprites; on the keyboard a keycap with\n  `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`'s text; after mouse use, a mouse icon with the bound button lit (for actions with a\n  mouse binding; else the keycap).\n- Icons are drawn once at boot into sprites at 9 px (prompt lines) and 16 px (How to Play): PlayStation ✕ (blue X on a\n  dark disc), ○ (red ring), □ (pink square), △ (green triangle), L1 R1 L2 R2, OPTIONS, CREATE, d-pad, sticks; Xbox A\n  (green), B (red), X (blue), Y (yellow), LB RB LT RT, Menu, View; keycaps sized to their text; a mouse with the left or\n  right half lit.\n- `promptLine(g, 'Hold {turbo} + {shoot} to DUNK', x, y, { player })` swaps `{action}` tokens for icons (`{move}` shows\n  the stick or WASD).\n- Settings → Button symbols (PlayStation | Xbox) sets `glyphs` on every player's input, including players who join\n  later. The pixel font has no ✕○□△, so canvas prompts always use the icons; the engine's HTML screens show its own text.\n\n### 11.3 Screen flow\n\n```\nBOOT → TITLE (\"PRESS START\") ──(10 s without input)──> ATTRACT ──(any input)──> back where it started\nTITLE → MAIN MENU: BLAM TOUR · EXHIBITION · BLAM CAMP · HALL OF BLAM · HOW TO PLAY · OPTIONS · ABOUT\n  BLAM TOUR  → CONTINUE TOUR | NEW TOUR → TEAM SELECT (your side) → LINEUP → [PROLOGUE] → TOUR MAP → stops…\n  EXHIBITION → JOIN (1–4 players, sides) → TEAM SELECT → LINEUP → COURT & RULES → MATCHUP CARD → MATCH → RESULTS\n  BLAM CAMP  → LESSONS → lesson…        HALL OF BLAM → tables        HOW TO PLAY → 3 pages\n  OPTIONS    → the engine's Settings (game.menu('settings'))           ABOUT → pages\nMATCH: TIP-OFF → Q1 → break → Q2 → HALFTIME REPORT → Q3 → break → Q4 → [OT…] → FINAL → RESULTS\nHub session: OWN CARD → MATCH (2 halves) → RESULTS overlay (the hub ends the round)\n```\n\nTen seconds without input on the title, the main menu or any pre-game menu screen starts the attract mode. Never show a\nmenu entry for something not built yet: entries arrive with their features.\n\n### 11.4 Screens\n\n- **Title:** the BASKETBLAM logo (`E.font.title` scale 5–6, \"BLAM\" bursting out of a comic star), the tagline, a\n  blinking PRESS START with its glyph, the Skybox at night behind it with two players looping an alley-oop, the version\n  (`E.versionLabel()` and the game's) small at the bottom. Keep the top right (110 × 60 CSS px) clear for the engine's\n  corner buttons.\n- **Main menu:** a big list on the left; a live preview panel on the right per entry (the tour map in miniature, two\n  teams squaring off, a coach's whistle...).\n- **Join:** four controller slots (P1–P4) in a centre column; each joined player slides its card to HOME (left) or AWAY\n  (right) with left/right and presses ✕ to be ready, ○ to leave; Start or ✕ on a free pad joins, Enter joins the\n  keyboard's left half and the engine's key (2) its right half (show which keys each half has). CPU fills empty seats.\n- **Team select:** two big team cards: logo, name, home court, three player portraits with their eight pip ratings\n  (icons), a CPU or P badge; left/right cycles, ✕ locks, △ shows the team's bio card.\n- **Lineup:** three player cards per team; each human picks theirs; the other starter is the best remaining juice.\n- **Court & rules** (Exhibition): five court cards (locked ones dim) with a preview; quarter length, CPU difficulty,\n  power-ups, twist; START.\n- **Matchup card** (\"TONIGHT'S MATCHUP\"): the starters' portraits facing off, ratings, the court; 6 s (each code step in\n  progress adds 2 s); the cheat-code window; ✕ skips.\n- **Break card and Halftime Report:** score, quarter leaders, a gag (halftime), juice bars and SUB buttons for human\n  teams; continues by itself after 8 s (halftime 12 s) unless someone opens subs.\n- **Results:** FINAL score huge; MVP portrait and a line; BLAM OF THE GAME (the best style play); page 2 a box score (4\n  rows × PTS REB AST STL BLK DNK); Continue (Tour) / Rematch / New Teams / Main Menu.\n- **Tour map:** a painted map: Neon Heights' skyline, the Pier on the coast, the Scrapyard inland, Kaboom Island off\n  shore, the Blam Dome on a hill; a dotted route; stop medallions (won: a W stamp and the score; next: pulsing; later:\n  dim) that the mouse can hover and click; a side panel with the tour score, the record and the next opponent.\n- **Hall of Blam:** top-10 tour scores (initials, team, score), and records: most points in a game, best dunk, tours won.\n- **How to Play:** page 1 a big controller (or keyboard) diagram with a callout per action, following the last device;\n  page 2 the rules (\"what you can and can't do\", §6.3) and Supernova; page 3 the courts' twists and the power-ups.\n- **About/Credits:** pages with one topic each (←/→ or L1/R1): CREDITS, SOURCE INFORMATION, TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE\n  FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK, ENGINE CHANGES, SECRETS (after the Tour). Large text (§16).\n\n### 11.5 The match HUD\n\n- **Top strip** (y 4–38): HOME panel at the left, AWAY at the right (`E.ui.box`, alpha .85, team colors), each with the\n  team name, the score (scale 2) and two player plates: name, a 3-px turbo bar, three heat pips, the power-up icon and\n  countdown, a P badge in the player's color for humans. Panel width = clamp((r.W − 84) / 2 − 8, 116, 170).\n- **Centre top:** the period (Q1–Q4, OT, SUDDEN BLAM), the game clock (scale 2), the shot clock in a box under it (red\n  under 5 s, a beep each second from 3).\n- **In the world:** a P1–P4 arrow tag over each human's player; a turbo ring under a player holding turbo; a soft ring\n  under the ball handler; edge arrows for humans off screen; the release meter by the shooter and the dunk-range ring\n  under a human handler holding turbo (Settings → Shot meter).\n- **Bottom centre:** the announcer's lower-third caption (portrait, name, two lines, non-modal). It is our own widget,\n  not an `E.Dialog`, so shoot and pass (which double as the engine's confirm) never skip it; `E.Dialog` is for story\n  beats only. Bottom left at the Pier: the windsock.\n\n### 11.6 Pause menu and settings\n\n- The engine's standard pause menu (an HTML Shell), themed: `new E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#fff7ec', paper:\n  '#140c24', accent: '#ff3ca6', muted: '#9a8fb8', danger: '#ff5a3a', line: '#3a2a5a', font: '700 1rem/1.35 \"Trebuchet\n  MS\", system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: '900 1.6rem/1 Impact, \"Arial Black\", system-ui' }, screens: { help:\n  HOW_TO_PLAY_HELP } })`, plus a CSS rule so its text scales for a TV (`.esh { font-size: clamp(18px, 2.6vh, 42px) }`);\n  check it in a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n- Pause items: Resume, How to Play, Restart Game (matches), Skip Cutscene (story), **Dev Mode**, then the standard\n  Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n- Game settings (group Game, through `menu.settings`): Button symbols (PlayStation | Xbox), CPU difficulty (Rookie | Pro\n  | All-Star | BLAM; Pro), Quarter length (1:00 | 1:30 | 2:00 | 3:00; 2:00), Power-ups (On | Off), Court twists (On |\n  Off), Jackpot Spot on every court (Off | On), Comeback assist (Off | Low | Normal), Commentary (Full | Big plays | Off),\n  Voice volume (slider), Camera (Broadcast | High), Shot meter (On | Off), Big heads (Off | On; defined once unlocked).\n  The standard ones stay (volume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, pixel scaling, filter, frame rate).\n\n### 11.7 Touch-only devices\n\n- Touch-only = `navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` and neither `(any-pointer: fine)` nor `(any-hover: hover)` matches, and no\n  gamepad and no key press seen yet. A `gamepadconnected` event or a first key press switches to normal play at once.\n- While touch-only: no touch controls at all (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, every scene `touch: []`); the title\n  shows **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** (scale 2, centred) and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n  `game.menu('settings')`); nothing else answers taps; after 10 s the attract mode runs as usual and keeps looping, and\n  a tap during it shows the notice and the button over it for 4 s instead of leaving.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Audio (every sound, song and voice made in code)\n\n### 12.1 Music\n\nEngine songs (`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, notes, on }] }`; Appendix C has a complete one), layers\nswitched with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`, jingles with `audio.sting`.\n\n| Song | Where | Feel | bpm | Key | Layers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `title` | title, main menu | funk anthem: slap bass, saw brass stabs, boom-bap | 108 | E minor | `hype` lead after 8 bars |\n| `menu` | pre-game menus | the anthem's bass and drums | 108 | E minor | – |\n| `skybox` | the Skybox | electro-funk, arpeggios | 116 | A minor | `nova` |\n| `pier` | the Pier | surf-funk, twangy pulse lead | 124 | D major | `nova` |\n| `scrapyard` | the Scrapyard | industrial boom-bap, metallic noise hits | 92 | C minor | `nova` |\n| `caldera` | the Caldera | tiki drums and bass, marimba-like triangle | 128 | G minor pentatonic | `nova` |\n| `dome` | the Blam Dome | arena rock-hop, saw power chords, big drums | 132 | E minor | `nova`, `overclock` (frantic arpeggio), `clutch` (more drums) |\n| `halftime` | halftime report | chip marching band | 120 | B♭ major | – |\n| `tourmap` | tour map | travel groove | 100 | F major | – |\n| `story` | cutscenes | tension bed: drones, sparse plucks | 84 | D minor | `villain` (organ) |\n| `camp` | Blam Camp | light practice loop | 104 | C major | – |\n| `credits` | ending, credits | the anthem in a major key | 112 | E major | – |\n\nStings: `tip`, `buzzer`, `nova`, `shatter`, `victory`, `defeat`, `unlock`, `sponsor` (a 4-s cheesy ad jingle). Dynamics:\nthe last 30 s of Q4 or overtime within 6 points bring in `clutch` and `audio.tempo(bpm + 6)`; Supernova brings `nova`;\nOverclock brings `overclock`; music dips 25% while a voice speaks. Tracks of different loop lengths phase against each\nother (the engine loops each on its own length); melody vol ≤ .08, bass ≤ .3, drums about .1.\n\n### 12.2 Sound effects\n\nDefined with `audio.define(name, voice)` (the engine's voices: `{ wave, freq, to, dur, vol, filter, vib, arp, step }`\nor a list of them); played through one policy function that sets volume by distance from the camera's centre.\n\n| Group | Sounds |\n|---|---|\n| ball | `dribble_asphalt`, `dribble_planks`, `dribble_concrete`, `dribble_stone`, `dribble_maple` (a sine thump 140 → 60 Hz, .07 s, plus a material tick of noise), `bounce`, `catch` (a soft slap), `release` (a short noise whoosh) |\n| hoop | `swish` (noise swept up 2 → 6 kHz, .25 s), `rim` (square 620 Hz + triangle 1240 Hz, fast decay, a click), `backboard` (triangle 160 → 110 Hz + a thud), `net_snap`, `slam` (sine 80 → 40 Hz boom + rim + crowd), `shatter` (a .5-s noise burst + 20 random high sine pings 2–6 kHz over .6 s) |\n| players | `squeak` (sine 2600 → 3400 Hz, .09 s, vibrato), `step`, `jump`, `land_heavy`, `turbo_loop` (low-pass noise while held), `shove` (punch + whoosh), `fall` (thump and rattle), `steal` (swipe + pop), `block` (slap + boom), `spin` (whoosh), `dizzy` (little tweets) |\n| match | `whistle`, `buzzer` (square 220 + 230 Hz beating, .9 s), `shotclock_beep`, `horn` (overtime), `crowd_roar`, `crowd_ooh`, `crowd_boo`, `camera_flash` (tiny clicks) |\n| power-ups and twists | `pu_spawn` (pulse arpeggio 0-4-7-12), `pu_pick` (the engine's `powerup`), `pu_end`, `jackpot`, `nova_on` (saw sweep 200 → 1600 Hz + crackle), `wind_gust` (band-passed noise sweep), `gull`, `oil_slip`, `rumble` (low noise 80–200 Hz, 1.5 s), `bomb_whistle` (sine 1200 → 400 Hz), `bomb_hit` (the engine's `explode`), `vent_puff`, `pyro`, `servo` (saw 300 → 500 Hz, vibrato), `reboot` (descending glitchy square) |\n| UI | the engine's `select`, `confirm`, `cancel`, `pause`; `code_ok` (a chime), `stamp` (the tour map's W stamp) |\n\n### 12.3 Voices: Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish (`12-audio-voice.js`)\n\n- `Voice.say(text, profile, { onEnd })` speaks a caption; `Voice.letter(ch, profile)` speaks while a Dialog types\n  (engine change 3). Text becomes syllables (a consonant cluster plus a vowel; digits and symbols skipped; spaces are\n  short gaps; punctuation longer ones).","numLines":400,"startLine":800,"totalLines":1605}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0157dxZrLB6Lz4rgJm5NNsAm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwZo95Mhg49kWXrpnwz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PkMRLAkE9bLdYU5iw55emb","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/PLAN.md","offset":1200,"limit":410},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18327,"cache_read_input_tokens":50828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18327},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad0c147-1299-4fc9-adba-2f06893c3033","uuid":"ca9ff6ff-d3fc-485e-b14b-fcdb4413c2e3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:09:14.542Z","request_id":"req_011CghwZnuvpUJYdAqJCF2hm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PkMRLAkE9bLdYU5iw55emb":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/PLAN.md","offset":1200,"limit":410}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PkMRLAkE9bLdYU5iw55emb","type":"tool_result","content":"1200\t- Each syllable: an oscillator (saw or pulse) at the profile's pitch through two band-pass filters at the vowel's\n1201\t  formants (a 800/1200, e 400/2000, i 300/2500, o 500/900, u 350/700, y 300/2200 Hz, × the profile's formant shift),\n1202\t  55–90 ms with a fast attack and release; consonants add a 20–30 ms noise burst (high-passed for s, f, sh, z; a low\n1203\t  thump for b, d, g; a click for t, k, p). Pitch: the profile's base, a gentle downdrift across the line, a rise at\n1204\t  \"?\", + 4 semitones and louder at \"!\", small random steps seeded by a hash of the text (the same line always sounds the\n1205\t  same).\n1206\t- Profiles (21): VINNIE (110 Hz, saw, fast 14 syllables/s, punchy), DEE DEE (230 Hz, pulse, 15/s, bright), GIGAWATT\n1207\t  (140 Hz, narrow nasal formants, 9/s, smug slides), REF ROSCOE, the 12 street players and the 3 bots (robot: ring\n1208\t  modulation by a 50-Hz sine, pitch quantized to steps), BLAMMO (very low, growl noise mixed in), the crowd chant (six\n1209\t  detuned copies).\n1210\t- Nodes connect to `audio.sfxBus` (engine change 4) through a voice gain (Settings → Voice volume). Headless: no audio,\n1211\t  but the syllable plan is still computed (tests read it).\n1212\t- Captions always show with the voice: the voice carries the tone, the caption the words.\n1213\t\n1214\t### 12.4 Crowd ambience\n1215\t\n1216\tA looping noise buffer generated in code (pink noise) through a band-pass (300–1200 Hz) with a slow LFO, its level and\n1217\tbrightness set by an excitement value 0..1 (close game, Q4, Supernova, a run of baskets). Events add swells (`roar` on\n1218\tdunks and shatters), an \"ooh\" (a formant sweep on noise) on near misses and big blocks, boos when the home team gets\n1219\tshoved or dunked on, and chants (\"DE-FENSE!\" style gibberish from the crowd profile) when a home team defends in the\n1220\tlast minute.\n1221\t\n1222\t---\n1223\t\n1224\t## 13. Attract mode (`45-attract.js`)\n1225\t\n1226\t- **Idle:** a timer resets on any input from any player (`input.anyPressed()` for every `game.players` entry, the stick\n1227\t  past its dead zone, a mouse move of more than 4 px, a click, a wheel, a key) and on `gamepadconnected`. Ten seconds\n1228\t  without input on the title, the main menu or any pre-game menu starts the attract mode (`game.go('attract')`).\n1229\t- **Any input exits** at once, back to the screen it interrupted (the title if it started there; menu screens keep their\n1230\t  choices in `S.menu`, so they come back as they were; the input is consumed so it doesn't also press a menu item),\n1231\t  except on a touch-only device (§11.7).\n1232\t- **What it plays:** \"CHANNEL BLAM DEMO\", a loop of five segments of real matches played by the CPU on both sides,\n1233\t  cheating freely (infinite turbo, wide dunk range, frequent power-ups, forced events), so every feature shows up:\n1234\t\n1235\t| # | Court, teams | Length | Forced and boosted |\n1236\t|---|---|---|---|\n1237\t| 1 | Skybox: Hightops vs Breakers | 35 s | tip-off; turbo dunks; an alley-oop at 12 s; the Jackpot Spot; a spin move |\n1238\t| 2 | Pier: Breakers vs Crushers | 30 s | a wind gust at 5 s; threes; steals; ROCKET KICKS and LASER SIGHT spawned |\n1239\t| 3 | Scrapyard: Crushers vs Magma | 30 s | shoves and a BLAM BOMB; an oil slip; a block and a putback |\n1240\t| 4 | Caldera: Magma vs Hightops | 35 s | an eruption at 6 s; a VOLCANO LAUNCH from a vent; a forced shatter and the sponsor break |\n1241\t| 5 | Blam Dome: Blambots vs All-Stars | 35 s | Supernova forced at 4 s (a 720), the Overclock, a POSTERIZED dunk, a BLAM-QUAKE, a reboot |\n1242\t\n1243\t  Between segments: a 2-s \"TONIGHT ON CHANNEL BLAM\" card; after segment 5 the Hall of Blam table (6 s), then the title\n1244\t  logo (4 s); then it loops. Segments start mid-game with a plausible score and clock.\n1245\t- **Director:** each segment is data: `{ court, home, away, seconds, score, quarter, cheats, script: [[t, action,\n1246\t  args]] }`; actions: `give(slot)`, `command(slot, 'dunk' | 'oop' | 'three' | 'spin' | 'shove' | 'steal' | 'block')`,\n1247\t  `spawn(powerup, near)`, `twist(kind)`, `nova(slot)`, `shatterNext()`, `overclock()`. The AI plays the rest. Captions\n1248\t  in the lower third name each feature as it happens (\"TURBO DUNK!\", \"ALLEY-OOP!\", \"SUPERNOVA!\"), plus \"DEMO · PRESS ANY\n1249\t  BUTTON\" (glyphs) blinking.\n1250\t- **Sound:** the attract plays music and effects at the user's volumes once audio has been unlocked (browsers allow\n1251\t  sound only after a gesture; before that it runs silently).\n1252\t\n1253\t---\n1254\t\n1255\t## 14. Dev mode (`46-dev.js`)\n1256\t\n1257\t**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item** (also `#dev` for tests; disabled in hub sessions). Choosing it resumes\n1258\tthe game with the **dev panel** docked on the right third of the screen. While the panel has the focus, the human\n1259\tplayers' slots are driven by CPU brains (the match keeps flowing, so every change shows live); Esc/○ or the pause key\n1260\tcloses the panel and gives control back. The panel is our own canvas UI (the same widgets as the menus), navigable by\n1261\tpad, keys and mouse; one tab at a time, at most 8 rows a page.\n1262\t\n1263\t| Tab | Contents |\n1264\t|---|---|\n1265\t| TUNING | every `TUNING` slider by group (Movement, Shooting, Dunks & Blocks, Defense, Supernova, CPU, Match, Physics, Courts), live; ← → or the mouse wheel change a value, △ resets one, RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS, SAVE AS MY DEFAULTS (`bb:tuning`), COPY AS JSON |\n1266\t| CHEATS | infinite turbo (P1 / everyone), always Supernova (HOME / AWAY), CPU passive, shots always in / always out / normal, unblockable dunks, one-shove knockdowns, big heads, power-ups every 5 s, twists on/off, freeze game clock, freeze shot clock, unlock everything, reset save data (asks first) |\n1267\t| MATCH | score ± for each team, quarter, clock, shot clock, give the ball to any slot, force a tip-off, end the quarter, end the game (win / loss), Supernova for any slot, shatter next dunk, spawn each power-up, place the Jackpot Spot, trigger each twist (gust, slicks, eruption, vent puff, Overclock, reboot), swap any slot to CPU or back |\n1268\t| SCENES | jump to: any court (Exhibition with chosen teams), any Tour stop, any story beat, credits, results, the attract mode (any segment), any Blam Camp lesson, the hub card preview, `#animlab`, `#shootaround` |\n1269\t| DEBUG | overlays: hitboxes (body radii, steal reach arcs, block hands, rim torus, backboard plane, ball), AI intents (text over each CPU: DRIVE, PASS→2, MARK #3, BOX OUT), shot chance at release (and the last shot's breakdown), ball path prediction, twist areas, event log (last 10 events), state snapshot |\n1270\t| TIME | game speed 0.1 / 0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2, freeze, step one frame (while frozen), slow motion on dunks on/off |\n1271\t| CAMERA | broadcast / high view, zoom, free camera (`cam.free`), reset |\n1272\t\n1273\tEvery slider shows its name, value, default and a one-line help text; changed values are marked with a dot.\n1274\t\n1275\t---\n1276\t\n1277\t## 15. Online: AI Hub (`50-hub.js`)\n1278\t\n1279\tFollows `vendor/hub-harness/README.md` (AI Hub Session Protocol v1). Outside a session (`AIHub.active` false, or\n1280\t`connect()` resolves `null`) the game is exactly the standalone game.\n1281\t\n1282\t### 15.1 Tags (in `<head>`, after the client script)\n1283\t\n1284\t```html\n1285\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1286\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1287\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1288\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n1289\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other crew over two halves\">\n1290\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □/Space shoot · ✕/E pass · R2/Shift turbo · ○/Q shove\">\n1291\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1292\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1293\t```\n1294\t\n1295\t### 15.2 The round: \"HUB SHOWDOWN\"\n1296\t\n1297\t- Straight into the round: no title, attract, menus or prompts. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode:\n1298\t  'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; build the match; `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start (no key press).\n1299\t- **Teams and seats:** seats 0 and 2 play for HOME, 1 and 3 for AWAY; empty slots are CPU (Pro). Teams and court come\n1300\t  from `AIHub.rng('roster')` (two different street crews; the court is HOME's), so every copy builds the same roster;\n1301\t  the host also sends it reliably once (`{ t: 'r', ... }`).\n1302\t- **Rules:** two halves of 1:30, a 3-s halftime card (no menus, no subs), power-ups and twists on, no cheats, no taunts\n1303\t  (they would be emotes). A tie at the end: 30 s of SUDDEN BLAM; still tied at time-up: a tie.\n1304\t- **Our own card** (until `start`): the court at night with both teams lined up; the hub's names over the players they\n1305\t  will control, in their seat colors, CPU over the rest; ready marks; how to win; this device's controls in its glyphs;\n1306\t  the countdown from the `card` event's `left` (PAUSED while `paused`). Enter, ✕ or a click on READY →\n1307\t  `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △, the T key or a click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')` (again takes it back). Nothing\n1308\t  on the card changes the round.\n1309\t- **Start:** on `start`, show a 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()`; the host starts the tip-off when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n1310\t- **No pausing the world:** match scenes are not pausable in a session and `autoPause` is off; Options or Esc (Options\n1311\t  only while Create is not held: Create + Options is the hub's) opens a small session overlay that does not stop the\n1312\t  simulation: sound volume, voice volume, button symbols, close. No Quit, Restart or title.\n1313\t- **End:** the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` once, when the game ends or on `time-up`\n1314\t  (at once, within `graceMs`): winners' remaining human ids in the first array, losers' in the second (a tie: one\n1315\t  array); `scores`: each human's team score; `stats`: `{ id: { PTS, DUNKS, STL, BLK } }`; `awards`: Dunk of the Round,\n1316\t  Pickpocket, Wall. With one human player add `won: true | false`. Before `finish` the host sends a reliable last\n1317\t  snapshot with `over: 1`. On `end`: stop input, stop the music and voices, freeze, show the final score until the hub\n1318\t  removes the game.\n1319\t- **Leaving:** on `leave`, that seat's player becomes CPU at once and stays in the game; the round goes on. If the host\n1320\t  leaves, the hub voids the round: clients show \"HOST LEFT\" and wait for `end`.\n1321\t- **Server:** with `AIHub.server` true the host copy has no local player, camera, sound or input: it runs the world with\n1322\t  every human slot from the network, draws only a small \"HOSTING\" text, and does everything else a host does.\n1323\t- **Failure:** if the engine can't run (its boot reports an error), call `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n1324\t\n1325\t### 15.3 Netcode (host-authoritative)\n1326\t\n1327\t- **Host:** runs the whole match as usual; each human seat's slot uses a `NetSource` fed by that seat's input messages.\n1328\t  Its own player (when it has one) uses local input.\n1329\t- **Client → host**, every 66 ms (15/s), unreliable: `{ t: 'i', s: seq, a: AIHub.time(), m: [mx, my] (×64, integers),\n1330\t  h: heldBits, e: [[eventId, actionBit, down 1 | up 0], ...the last 8 edges] }`. The host applies the stick and held bits\n1331\t  and each edge event once (by id), in order, so a lost packet loses nothing.\n1332\t- **Host → all**, every 66 ms, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: seq, a: AIHub.time(), g: [phase, period,\n1333\t  clock×10, shot×10, scoreH, scoreA, possession, flags], b: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner, state], p: [[x, y, z, vx, vy,\n1334\t  facing×100, state, stateT×100, turbo×100, flags], ×4], ev: [[id, type, ...args] for events of the last second] }`.\n1335\t  Positions are rounded to integers.\n1336\t- **Clients** render remote things 100 ms in the past, interpolating between snapshots (snapping discrete states). Their\n1337\t  own player's running is predicted locally from its stick with the same movement code, and pulled toward the host's\n1338\t  position (blend 15% a frame; snap beyond 48; follow the host entirely during knockdowns, dunks, shots and other\n1339\t  non-running states). The ball, possession and every outcome come only from the host. Each event id plays its sounds,\n1340\t  captions and effects once.\n1341\t- **Budget:** at most 15 messages a second from each copy plus rare reliable ones (roster, over), under the client's\n1342\t  20/s limit; every message JSON and under 16 KB. If no snapshot arrives for 1 s, clients show \"WAITING FOR HOST\".\n1343\t- The host's tab hidden freezes the world (rAF stops); the hub voids the round after 20 s: accept it.\n1344\t\n1345\t### 15.4 What the harness checks (it must pass every scenario)\n1346\t\n1347\t`harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with\n1348\t`&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server`; use `&limit=45` to keep them short. It checks the tags, `connect`,\n1349\t`ready` with no key press, Enter on our card answering Ready, the start, traffic both ways, a server copy running the\n1350\tworld, a player leaving (with 3+ players the last one leaves), the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, every copy told\n1351\tthe round ended, no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets. Pass = `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` once\n1352\t`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`.\n1353\t\n1354\t---\n1355\t\n1356\t## 16. About/Credits and the exit interview\n1357\t\n1358\tThe About screen's pages (§11.4) and the final chat reply carry, as TASK.md requires (write \"unknown\" for anything not\n1359\tconfirmed):\n1360\t\n1361\t- **Source Information:** Date (TASK.md's: 2026-11-03 17:48:22); Source (\"Basketball, in the over-the-top arcade\n1362\t  style (genre inspiration; an original game)\"); Plan (`PLAN.md`); Genre and Perspective (arcade sports, 2-on-2\n1363\t  basketball; side-on broadcast camera, orthographic pitch 30°, optional High camera); Tech (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 modified,\n1364\t  AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node, Playwright 1.63, Python http.server for\n1365\t  tests); Art Direction; Animation; Audio; Online; Testing; Research; Environment (Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux;\n1366\t  browser unknown); Model (as TASK.md gives it, corrected if another model builds); Usage (estimates only if available).\n1367\t- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** the builder's answers to TASK.md's questions, in order.\n1368\t- **Credits:** the game; the engine (my-3D2dge, MIT); the AI Hub client; \"every sound, song and voice made in code\";\n1369\t  the engine changes (§5) with their reasons.\n1370\t\n1371\t`exit-interview.json` goes in the root beside the HTML, exactly in TASK.md's shape, plain text, every value filled, and\n1372\tchecked with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Its `aiHub` block:\n1373\tname `BASKETBLAM`, tagline `No fouls. No mercy. All BLAM.`, a one-to-two-sentence description, type `Game`, genre\n1374\t`Sports`, source `Basketball (over-the-top arcade style)`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags such\n1375\tas `[\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]`.\n1376\t\n1377\t---\n1378\t\n1379\t## 17. Build order and milestones\n1380\t\n1381\tEach milestone ends with its tests passing (§19) and the game complete for what it contains: no menu entry, button or\n1382\tscreen for anything not built yet, no TODOs. Commit nothing outside the dev folder except the deliverables.\n1383\t\n1384\t| # | Milestone | Build | Done when |\n1385\t|---|---|---|---|\n1386\t| M0 | Pipeline | setup (§3); `tools/build.mjs` (fragments → `build/game.js`, `build/index.html`, the root bundle with the client first in `<head>`, `</script` escaped); `tests/run.mjs` and `helpers.mjs`; scenes table with a boot and an empty title; `game.debug` | `node tests/run.mjs` prints one line; the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors (`handoff/tools/check.mjs`) |\n1387\t| M1 | Court, ball, hoops, camera | the arena TileMap and the Skybox floor painter with lines; the broadcast view; hoop drawing (stanchion, cheated glass, rim halves, net springs); ball physics with rim, board, floor and walls; scoring detection; the camera director; `#shootaround` (a bench that fires seeded shots) | physics tests pass (made rate = decided rate ± 3%, no tunneling); screenshots of the ball in front of, inside and behind the net look right |\n1388\t| M2 | A playable 2-on-2 | player entity, the rig factory with shorts (engine change 1), movement and turbo, the dribble, possession, passes, jump shots with the release meter, 2/3 points, inbounds, both clocks, quarters, the match flow, a first CPU brain, HUD v1, `Cmd` and input sources, `serializeMatch`/`applySnapshot`, the event bus, tuning store | 1 player plays a whole game against the CPU on the Skybox; rules tests pass; a fake-hub test shows a second instance rendering the match from snapshots |\n1389\t| M3 | The arcade layer | layups, the 12 dunks with choreography and the dunk cam, alley-oops, putbacks, posterized, steals, shoves and knockdowns, spin moves, blocks, goaltending, rebounds and box-outs, the tip-off, Supernova, shatter and the sponsor break, juice and subs, stats and style points, banners and every effect (§9), `#animlab`, a first dev panel (TUNING with reset) | mechanics tests pass; filmstrips of every dunk, shove, block and celebration read well |\n1390\t| M4 | CPU AI | the full brains (§8), difficulty table, comeback, teammate commands, twist and power-up awareness | AI soak tests pass (§19); difficulty ordering holds |\n1391\t| M5 | Audio | every sound effect, the songs and stings, crowd ambience, the voice synth (engine changes 3 and 4) and the announcer system with captions | audio tests pass; in Chromium the audio smoke test finds sound and no errors |\n1392\t| M6 | Screens and flows | the UI kit, glyph icons and prompt lines, title, main menu, join (1–4), team select, lineup, court & rules, matchup card with codes, break cards, halftime report, results, Hall of Blam, How to Play, Options, About/Credits (with its text written as the build goes), touch-only notice, the themed pause menu and settings | flow and UI tests pass; screenshots at 1920×1080 and 390×844@3 read at a glance |\n1393\t| M7 | Content | the other four courts (floors, backdrops, silhouettes, props and new shapes, crowds, lights, weather) and their twists; all teams and rigs (engine change 2: hair); power-ups; the Jackpot Spot | content lint passes; an AI soak on every court; screenshots of each court |\n1394\t| M8 | Tour, story, camp | tour map, the prologue and every beat (§10.6), the boss mechanics, ending and credits, unlocks, autosave and CONTINUE TOUR, Hall of Blam entry, Blam Camp's 10 lessons | the scripted Tour playthrough and the camp tests pass |\n1395\t| M9 | Attract and dev mode | the attract director with its 5 segments, the full dev panel (§14) | attract and dev tests pass |\n1396\t| M10 | AI Hub | the card, host, client, server, leave, time-up, end, the session overlay | net tests and all four harness scenarios pass |\n1397\t| M11 | Finish | a balance pass with the dev sliders (scores of 30–60 per team in a 2:00-quarter game, about one dunk in three baskets, a Supernova most games), polish, a full screenshot review, the final bundle, About pages and the chat reply's sections, `exit-interview.json` | every test passes; the Definition of Done (§20) is all yes |\n1398\t\n1399\tOrder inside a milestone: data and rules first, then visuals, then tests that pin the behavior. Write each test with the\n1400\tcode it covers, and rerun a suite only after changing code it covers; run everything before closing a milestone.\n1401\t\n1402\t---\n1403\t\n1404\t## 18. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1405\t\n1406\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1407\t|---|---|---|\n1408\t| Shot and rim physics | balls tunnelling through the rim, odd bounces, made rates drifting from the decided chance | decide-then-fly (§6.7); 4× substeps near rims; the M1 `#shootaround` bench with hundreds of seeded shots checked against the decided outcome; tune `rimBounce` there |\n1409\t| Basketball animation on a procedural rig | IK hands that pop, dribbles out of sync, dunks that look stiff | the pose layer over `solvePose` with eased keys; dribble driven by the ball's own phase; `#animlab` and filmstrips from M2; clips are data, so iterate quickly |\n1410\t| Depth sorting around the hoop | ball, rim, net and glass drawn in the wrong order | split rim and net into back and front halves queued at different depths; screenshots of the ball at known positions (in front, inside, behind, on the rim) in M1 |\n1411\t| Backboards edge-on in an orthographic side view | an invisible glass, a weak look | the cheated, turned panel (§9.3), decided up front |\n1412\t| CPU that is dull, stuck or broken | the whole game rests on it | headless AI-vs-AI soaks on every court from M4 with stall detectors (shot clock violations, players not moving, nobody scoring) and difficulty-ordering checks |\n1413\t| Shared world over the hub | 20 messages a second, latency, loss, players leaving, a server copy | one `Cmd` path and snapshot functions from M2; a fake-hub test in M2; redundant edge events; small snapshots; the harness's four scenarios in M10 |\n1414\t| The standard pause stopping a hub round | the engine pauses on Start, on focus loss | in a session: `menu: false`, `autoPause: false`, unpausable scenes, our own non-pausing overlay (§15.2) |\n1415\t| Scope (5 courts, 22 rigs, a story) | running out of time with half-built content | data registries, a playable complete game by M3, content in M7 as data entries; never show what isn't built |\n1416\t| 10-foot readability and prompts | small text, wrong glyphs | the rules in §11.1; glyph unit tests per device and style; 1920×1080 screenshots |\n1417\t| Gibberish voice quality | it can sound like noise | formant pairs per vowel, per-character profiles, a seeded contour; listen in the browser once per profile; keep captions always on |\n1418\t| Touch-only detection | touchscreen laptops misdetected | require no fine pointer and no hover; switch back on a key press or a gamepad |\n1419\t| Determinism | engine internals use `Math.random` | gameplay draws from `S.rng`; tests seed `Math.random` too; the proof hashes twice |\n1420\t| The shared machine | ports and processes of other agents; a full /tmp | port 0 on 127.0.0.1, PID-only cleanup, `TMPDIR` inside the dev folder when needed |\n1421\t\n1422\t---\n1423\t\n1424\t## 19. Testing\n1425\t\n1426\t### 19.1 The one command\n1427\t\n1428\t`node tests/run.mjs [suite ...] [--quick]` (in the dev folder) runs the suites named, or all of them; `--quick` skips the\n1429\tbrowser and hub suites. It prints **only failures** (`FAIL <suite>.<test>: <what was expected, what happened, a short\n1430\tsnapshot>`) and then **one line**: `BASKETBLAM tests: 231 passed, 0 failed (41.8 s)`. Exit code 1 on any failure.\n1431\t\n1432\t- **Headless suites** load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `build/game.js` (and `vendor/aihub-session.js` first, as the page\n1433\t  does) into a fresh `node:vm` context with the stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`)\n1434\t  plus `removeEventListener`, `matchMedia` (configurable), `navigator` (`maxTouchPoints`, `getGamepads`) and a seeded\n1435\t  `Math.random`. They drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap / hold`, `game.addPlayer`,\n1436\t  `input.feed(...)` (mouse) and read `game.debug.snapshot()` and the event log.\n1437\t- **Bots:** a test \"plays\" a human seat by driving the real input actions from the CPU brain's own judgment (as\n1438\t  `kits/sports.js`'s `bot()` does), so the full input path is exercised.\n1439\t- Long runs use short quarters (`tune('quarterLength', 20)`), except one full-length game.\n1440\t\n1441\t### 19.2 Suites and what they check\n1442\t\n1443\t| Suite | Checks |\n1444\t|---|---|\n1445\t| `content` | every registry entry is valid: 6 teams × 3 players with 8 ratings in 1..10, rig specs, voices, taunts; 5 courts with every field; 12 dunks; 6 power-ups; 7 codes; line banks with ≥ 10 lines, ≤ 60 characters, only known slots; story beats name existing speakers; every setting has a default; every action has an icon on every device and style |\n1446\t| `physics` | floor bounce decay; 500 seeded \"made\" shots go in ≥ 97% and 500 \"missed\" ≤ 3%; banks off the glass; a 900 u/s ball never tunnels through rim or board; a basket counts only downward and once; the ball never leaves the arena |\n1447\t| `rules` | 2 vs 3 points by takeoff just inside / outside the arc and in the corners; dunk 2; goaltending awards the basket; Jackpot + 2; Gold Ball doubles; shot clock expiry is a turnover; a made basket gives the other team the inbound; the shot clock resets on rim contact; a release before the buzzer counts, after doesn't; overtime on a tie; SUDDEN BLAM after two; tip-off winner gets the ball; the alternating arrow for Q2–Q4 |\n1448\t| `mechanics` | turbo drain and refill; speed by ZOOM; steal rates by angle within expected bands over 1,000 seeded tries; shoves knock down and fumble; a spin move breaks steals and ankles; blocks succeed when timed and fail when late; layup vs dunk choice; dunk choice by distance and SLAM; alley-oop from pass to slam; putback; posterized; Supernova on after 3 straight, off after an opposing basket, 4 more baskets or 40 s; shatter → sponsor break → inbound; juice falls and subs apply; each power-up's effect and expiry; wind bends a shot but keeps its decided outcome; oil slicks slide and slip; lava bombs knock down; vents launch; Overclock at Q4; reboot after two knockdowns |\n1449\t| `ai` | 20 seeded CPU-vs-CPU games per court (20-s quarters): no errors; every team scores; scores in a sane band; ≤ 2 shot clock violations a game; no player still for more than 6 s of live play; across the batch the CPU dunks, shoots threes, steals, shoves, blocks, throws oops and uses power-ups; BLAM beats Rookie in ≥ 16 of 20 |\n1450\t| `flow` | boot → title; 10 s idle on the title, the main menu and the join screen → attract; a key, a pad button, a mouse click and a stick push each leave it in one step, back to the screen it interrupted with its choices intact; every main-menu entry reaches a working screen by keyboard, by pad and by mouse; Exhibition with 1, 2, 3 and 4 players (addPlayer) gives each the right player and side; pause shows Dev Mode, How to Play and (in a match) Restart; results' buttons work; Hall of Blam initials entry |\n1451\t| `tour` | **the scripted playthrough of the whole game**: a new Tour with a bot human, through the prologue, all three stops and the final, every beat seen in order, the reveal, the Overclock, the ending, credits, unlocks granted, Hall of Blam entry; it rematches a lost stop (exercising the loss path); CONTINUE TOUR after reloading the context mid-tour resumes at the right stop |\n1452\t| `camp` | every lesson completes with scripted input and saves its completion; skipping works; its prompts name the right keys or buttons per device |\n1453\t| `attract` | three full loops of every segment without errors; each segment's showcase events happen (event log); any input leaves within a step; touch-only: the loop continues and a tap shows the notice |\n1454\t| `dev` | the pause menu's Dev Mode opens the panel; each slider changes and clamps its value and the game reacts (e.g. `runSpeed` × 1.5 → 50% more distance in a second); RESET ALL restores every default; each cheat and match action works; every SCENES jump lands in its scene; overlays draw without errors (in the browser suite) |\n1455\t| `ui` | glyph icons for every action × keyboard, mouse, PlayStation and Xbox; prompts follow `lastDevice` per player; Button symbols changes every player's glyphs (and a later joiner's); settings defaults; touch-only detection on and off (stubbed `matchMedia` and `navigator`) and its switch-back on a key or gamepad |\n1456\t| `audio` | every song's tokens parse (no engine warnings); every sound name used exists; the voice's syllable plan for sample lines (count, timing, the \"!\" and \"?\" contours); no audio calls fail headless |\n1457\t| `net` | with `tests/fakehub.mjs` (2–4 game contexts sharing a simulated network with latency and loss, an `AIHub` stub per copy): clients' inputs move their players on the host; snapshots apply and the final scores agree; each event plays once; a leaver's player turns CPU; time-up → `finish` within the grace with valid standings; host leaving → clients show the void; server mode runs the world with no local player; every copy stays under 20 messages a second and unreliable messages under 1,200 bytes; the card answers Ready on Enter and More time on △ |\n1458\t| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same hash twice (the proof) |\n1459\t| `bundle` | the root HTML exists with the exact name; the client is the first script in `<head>`, byte-identical to `vendor/aihub-session.js`; the hub tags are there; no external URLs are loaded; its inline scripts run headless and reach the title |\n1460\t| `browser` (Playwright, `file://`) | `handoff/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle passes (no errors, the screen filled, look notes read and acted on); every deep link renders without errors; the audio smoke test (after a synthetic key press the AudioContext runs, a voice line and a song play without errors); the screenshot set below is written |\n1461\t| `hub` (Playwright + a 127.0.0.1 port-0 server) | the four harness scenarios of §15.4 pass; the server is checked to serve our page first and is stopped by its PID |\n1462\t\n1463\t### 19.3 Screenshots (for what scripts can't judge)\n1464\t\n1465\tWritten to `check-output/` by the browser suite at 1920×1080 (and 1280×720): the title; the main menu; join with 4\n1466\tplayers; team select; the matchup card; each court in play (5); a dunk at its apex with the dunk cam; a shatter; the\n1467\tSupernova trail; the hoop with the ball in front of, inside and behind the net; the halftime report; results; the tour\n1468\tmap; a story beat with portraits; the dev panel on each tab; the pause menu with Dev Mode; How to Play (pad and keyboard);\n1469\tAbout pages; the hub card; the touch-only title at 390×844@3. Look at every one: TV readability, the look target\n1470\t(§2), nothing clipped by the corner buttons. Filmstrips (`handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) for every dunk, the\n1471\tshove and knockdown, the block, the jump shot and the celebrations.\n1472\t\n1473\t---\n1474\t\n1475\t## 20. Definition of done (TASK.md, line by line)\n1476\t\n1477\t- [ ] The title is BASKETBLAM, from the RNG pick; the deliverable and the dev folder have TASK.md's exact names.\n1478\t- [ ] One self-contained HTML in the root; it runs from `file://` and inside the hub; no runtime network requests.\n1479\t- [ ] Built on the my-3D2dge handoff; engine changes marked and listed; the engine's native look and rig animation are\n1480\t      the base, with our new assets (courts, shapes, hoops, crowd, icons) and animations (§7).\n1481\t- [ ] All music, effects and voices made in code; voices are gibberish with captions.\n1482\t- [ ] AI Hub: tags, client first in `<head>`, own card, shared world, every harness scenario passing; the game unchanged\n1483\t      on its own.\n1484\t- [ ] Every system and mechanic in §6–§9 works; all content in §10 is in; every screen in §11 exists and works by pad,\n1485\t      keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device with PlayStation glyphs and an Xbox option.\n1486\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu, with live sliders and reset to defaults, and the tools in §14.\n1487\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input leaves; it shows every feature.\n1488\t- [ ] Touch-only devices: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract running.\n1489\t- [ ] Narrative and announcer writing in the over-the-top arcade broadcast style (§10.6–10.7).\n1490\t- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders, stubbed features or dead menu entries (grep the source for TODO, FIXME, XXX, \"placeholder\").\n1491\t- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` passes, including the scripted playthrough of the whole Tour; screenshots reviewed.\n1492\t- [ ] The About/Credits screen and the final chat reply carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and\n1493\t      Prompt Feedback; `exit-interview.json` is beside the HTML, in TASK.md's shape, and parses.\n1494\t- [ ] Only processes you started were stopped, by PID; temporary folders removed.\n1495\t\n1496\t---\n1497\t\n1498\t## Appendix A. Tuning defaults (`01-tuning.js`; every one a live dev slider)\n1499\t\n1500\t| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Notes |\n1501\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1502\t| Movement | `runSpeed` | 108 | 60–160 | u/s before ZOOM |\n1503\t| | `accel` | 900 | 300–2000 | u/s² |\n1504\t| | `turboMult` | 1.5 | 1.0–2.2 | |\n1505\t| | `turboDrain` | 0.30 | 0.05–0.8 | per second held and moving |\n1506\t| | `turboRefill` | 0.20 | 0.05–0.8 | per second |\n1507\t| | `turboRefillDelay` | 0.35 | 0–1.5 | s |\n1508\t| | `playerGravity` | 900 | 500–1500 | |\n1509\t| | `jumpShotVz` | 250 | 150–400 | before SWAT |\n1510\t| Shooting | `shotSkill` | 1.0 | 0.4–1.6 | × every make chance |\n1511\t| | `threeSkill` | 1.0 | 0.4–1.6 | × three-point chance |\n1512\t| | `perfectWindow` | 0.10 | 0.03–0.30 | s, full width |\n1513\t| | `perfectBonus` | 0.15 | 0–0.4 | |\n1514\t| | `badReleasePenalty` | 0.30 | 0–0.6 | |\n1515\t| | `contestPenalty` | 0.40 | 0–0.8 | |\n1516\t| | `shotArc` | 1.0 | 0.6–1.6 | × apex height |\n1517\t| Dunks & blocks | `dunkRange` | 150 | 60–300 | from the rim, before SLAM |\n1518\t| | `dunkGravity` | 520 | 300–900 | |\n1519\t| | `dunkApex` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | |\n1520\t| | `dunkHang` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × flight time |\n1521\t| | `dunkSlowMo` | 0.45 | 0.1–1.0 | time scale at the apex (1 = off) |\n1522\t| | `blockReach` | 14 | 6–30 | before SWAT |\n1523\t| | `blockChance` | 1.0 | 0–2 | |\n1524\t| | `shatterChance` | 1.0 | 0–5 | |\n1525\t| Defense | `stealChance` | 0.30 | 0–0.9 | |\n1526\t| | `stealReach` | 18 | 8–36 | |\n1527\t| | `stealCooldown` | 0.6 | 0.1–2 | s |\n1528\t| | `shoveForce` | 220 | 60–500 | |\n1529\t| | `shoveCost` | 0.25 | 0–0.8 | turbo |\n1530\t| | `shoveCooldown` | 1.0 | 0.2–3 | s |\n1531\t| | `shoveFumble` | 0.6 | 0–1 | |\n1532\t| | `knockdownTime` | 0.8 | 0.2–2 | s |\n1533\t| | `spinCost` | 0.2 | 0–0.6 | turbo |\n1534\t| | `spinCooldown` | 1.5 | 0.3–4 | s |\n1535\t| Supernova | `novaBaskets` | 3 | 2–6 | to ignite |\n1536\t| | `novaMaxBaskets` | 4 | 1–10 | |\n1537\t| | `novaTime` | 40 | 10–120 | s of game clock |\n1538\t| | `novaShotBonus` | 0.25 | 0–0.6 | |\n1539\t| CPU | `cpuSkill` | 0 | −0.5–0.5 | offset on decision quality |\n1540\t| | `cpuReaction` | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | × reaction delays |\n1541\t| | `cpuAggression` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × steal and shove rates |\n1542\t| | `comeback` | 0.35 | 0–1 | |\n1543\t| Match | `quarterLength` | from the mode | 20–300 | s; the running match's (Exhibition 120, Tour 90, hub halves 90) |\n1544\t| | `shotClock` | 20 | 8–30 | s |\n1545\t| | `gameSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–1.5 | `game.timeScale` outside effects |\n1546\t| | `fatigue` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × juice loss |\n1547\t| Physics | `ballGravity` | 760 | 400–1200 | |\n1548\t| | `ballBounce` | 0.62 | 0.3–0.9 | |\n1549\t| | `rimBounce` | 0.45 | 0.2–0.8 | |\n1550\t| | `boardBounce` | 0.55 | 0.2–0.9 | |\n1551\t| Courts | `powerupInterval` | 22 | 6–60 | s |\n1552\t| | `hazardInterval` | 1.0 | 0.25–4 | × twist timers |\n1553\t| | `windStrength` | 140 | 0–300 | u/s² at full gust |\n1554\t| | `jackpotBonus` | 2 | 0–5 | points |\n1555\t\n1556\t## Appendix B. Data shapes\n1557\t\n1558\t```js\n1559\tdef('team', 'hightops', { name: 'NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS', short: 'HIGHTOPS', colors: { jersey: '#ff3ca6', trim: '#2de2ff',\n1560\t  shorts: '#1a1420', sneaker: '#f4f4f4', sock: '#2de2ff' }, logo: LOGO_SNEAKER, court: 'skybox', locked: false,\n1561\t  players: ['volt', 'bigrumble', 'pixel'], captainLines: { /* §10.6 replies by opponent */ } });\n1562\tdef('player', 'volt', { name: 'VOLT', team: 'hightops', number: 7, role: 'high-flyer',\n1563\t  ratings: { zoom: 9, splash: 5, deep: 4, slam: 9, dime: 6, swipe: 6, swat: 4, bump: 3 },\n1564\t  rig: { build: 'heroic', size: 1.65, hair: 'ponytail', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#ff3ca6' }, skin: '#8a5a3c', hairColor: '#3ab0ff' },\n1565\t  voice: 'volt', taunt: 'raiseRoof', celebrations: ['raiseRoof', 'airplane', 'pointSky'], barks: ['Too slow!', 'Catch me!'] });\n1566\tdef('court', 'skybox', { name: 'THE SKYBOX', floor: paintAsphalt, lines: { main: '#2de2ff', paint: '#ff3ca6' },\n1567\t  logo: LOGO_SNEAKER, backdrop: { sky: [...], stars: 60, moon: {...}, layers: [...] }, silhouettes: drawSkyline,\n1568\t  props: [['fence-chain', 200, -40, { params: { len: 400 } }], ['streetlamp', -48, -24]], crowd: ['#ff3ca6', '#2de2ff', '#1a1a1a', '#ffd23a'],\n1569\t  ambient: .45, lights: skyboxLights, weather: null, dribble: 'dribble_asphalt', music: 'skybox', twist: 'jackpot' });\n1570\tdef('dunk', 'windmill', { banner: 'WINDMILL!', slam: 7, dist: [50, 150], hands: 1, spin: 0, flip: 0, apexAbove: 40,\n1571\t  keys: [[0, { R: [4, 2, 20] }], [.3, { R: [0, 7, 14] }], [.55, { R: [-4, 4, 36] }], [.8, { R: [3, 2, 46] }], [.9, { R: [8, 1, 30], slam: true }]],\n1572\t  bonus: 100, lines: 'dunkPower' });\n1573\tdef('lines', 'steal', ['PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!', '{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!' /* ... ≥ 10 */]);\n1574\tdef('beat', 'reveal', { stage: 'dome-court', music: 'story', cast: ['gigawatt', 'dunkatron', 'swatbot', '{CAPTAIN}'],\n1575\t  lines: [['vinnie', 'THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!'], ['gigawatt', 'Congratulations...'] /* ... */],\n1576\t  camera: [[0, 'wide'], [2, 'gigawatt'], [5, 'bots']] });\n1577\tdef('powerup', 'rocket', { name: 'ROCKET KICKS', icon: ICON_ROCKET, color: '#ff7a2a', seconds: 15, apply(p) {...}, remove(p) {...} });\n1578\tdef('attract', 'seg4', { court: 'caldera', home: 'magma', away: 'hightops', seconds: 35, score: [22, 19], quarter: 3,\n1579\t  cheats: { infiniteTurbo: true, dunkRange: 220 }, script: [[6, 'twist', 'eruption'], [14, 'command', [0, 'vent']], [24, 'shatterNext']] });\n1580\t```\n1581\t\n1582\tA content lint (`content` suite) validates every entry at boot in dev builds and in tests, with messages that name the\n1583\tentry and the field.\n1584\t\n1585\t## Appendix C. A complete song in the engine's format (the `title` anthem)\n1586\t\n1587\t```js\n1588\tconst TITLE_SONG = { bpm: 108, steps: 4, tracks: [   // steps: 4 a beat, so a bar is 16 tokens\n1589\t  { name: 'bass', wave: 'square', vol: .22, notes:\n1590\t    'E2 . E3 . . E2 G2 . A2 . . B2 . A2 G2 . | E2 . E3 . . E2 G2 . D3 . C3 . B2 . G2 A2 |' },\n1591\t  { name: 'stabs', wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes:\n1592\t    '. . . . E4 . . . . . . . G4 - . . | . . . . E4 . . . . . . . A4 - B4 . |' },\n1593\t  { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes:\n1594\t    'k . h . s . h k . k h . s . h h | k . h . s . h k . k h . s h o . |' },\n1595\t  { name: 'hype', wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes:   // audio.layer('hype', 1, 1) after 8 bars\n1596\t    'B4 - - . A4 G4 . E4 - . . . . . . . | D5 - - . B4 A4 . G4 - . A4 . B4 - - . |' }\n1597\t] };\n1598\t```\n1599\t\n1600\tEvery other song follows this form (§12.1's table gives each one's feel, tempo, key and layers); check that the engine\n1601\taccepts each wave name and token (it warns on unknown ones) and listen to each in the browser once.\n1602\t\n1603\t*End of plan.*\n1604\t\n1605\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad0c147-1299-4fc9-adba-2f06893c3033","uuid":"7dc988b6-efe8-4dab-9701-3b0581a635ab","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:09:14.691Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Each syllable: an oscillator (saw or pulse) at the profile's pitch through two band-pass filters at the vowel's\n  formants (a 800/1200, e 400/2000, i 300/2500, o 500/900, u 350/700, y 300/2200 Hz, × the profile's formant shift),\n  55–90 ms with a fast attack and release; consonants add a 20–30 ms noise burst (high-passed for s, f, sh, z; a low\n  thump for b, d, g; a click for t, k, p). Pitch: the profile's base, a gentle downdrift across the line, a rise at\n  \"?\", + 4 semitones and louder at \"!\", small random steps seeded by a hash of the text (the same line always sounds the\n  same).\n- Profiles (21): VINNIE (110 Hz, saw, fast 14 syllables/s, punchy), DEE DEE (230 Hz, pulse, 15/s, bright), GIGAWATT\n  (140 Hz, narrow nasal formants, 9/s, smug slides), REF ROSCOE, the 12 street players and the 3 bots (robot: ring\n  modulation by a 50-Hz sine, pitch quantized to steps), BLAMMO (very low, growl noise mixed in), the crowd chant (six\n  detuned copies).\n- Nodes connect to `audio.sfxBus` (engine change 4) through a voice gain (Settings → Voice volume). Headless: no audio,\n  but the syllable plan is still computed (tests read it).\n- Captions always show with the voice: the voice carries the tone, the caption the words.\n\n### 12.4 Crowd ambience\n\nA looping noise buffer generated in code (pink noise) through a band-pass (300–1200 Hz) with a slow LFO, its level and\nbrightness set by an excitement value 0..1 (close game, Q4, Supernova, a run of baskets). Events add swells (`roar` on\ndunks and shatters), an \"ooh\" (a formant sweep on noise) on near misses and big blocks, boos when the home team gets\nshoved or dunked on, and chants (\"DE-FENSE!\" style gibberish from the crowd profile) when a home team defends in the\nlast minute.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Attract mode (`45-attract.js`)\n\n- **Idle:** a timer resets on any input from any player (`input.anyPressed()` for every `game.players` entry, the stick\n  past its dead zone, a mouse move of more than 4 px, a click, a wheel, a key) and on `gamepadconnected`. Ten seconds\n  without input on the title, the main menu or any pre-game menu starts the attract mode (`game.go('attract')`).\n- **Any input exits** at once, back to the screen it interrupted (the title if it started there; menu screens keep their\n  choices in `S.menu`, so they come back as they were; the input is consumed so it doesn't also press a menu item),\n  except on a touch-only device (§11.7).\n- **What it plays:** \"CHANNEL BLAM DEMO\", a loop of five segments of real matches played by the CPU on both sides,\n  cheating freely (infinite turbo, wide dunk range, frequent power-ups, forced events), so every feature shows up:\n\n| # | Court, teams | Length | Forced and boosted |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Skybox: Hightops vs Breakers | 35 s | tip-off; turbo dunks; an alley-oop at 12 s; the Jackpot Spot; a spin move |\n| 2 | Pier: Breakers vs Crushers | 30 s | a wind gust at 5 s; threes; steals; ROCKET KICKS and LASER SIGHT spawned |\n| 3 | Scrapyard: Crushers vs Magma | 30 s | shoves and a BLAM BOMB; an oil slip; a block and a putback |\n| 4 | Caldera: Magma vs Hightops | 35 s | an eruption at 6 s; a VOLCANO LAUNCH from a vent; a forced shatter and the sponsor break |\n| 5 | Blam Dome: Blambots vs All-Stars | 35 s | Supernova forced at 4 s (a 720), the Overclock, a POSTERIZED dunk, a BLAM-QUAKE, a reboot |\n\n  Between segments: a 2-s \"TONIGHT ON CHANNEL BLAM\" card; after segment 5 the Hall of Blam table (6 s), then the title\n  logo (4 s); then it loops. Segments start mid-game with a plausible score and clock.\n- **Director:** each segment is data: `{ court, home, away, seconds, score, quarter, cheats, script: [[t, action,\n  args]] }`; actions: `give(slot)`, `command(slot, 'dunk' | 'oop' | 'three' | 'spin' | 'shove' | 'steal' | 'block')`,\n  `spawn(powerup, near)`, `twist(kind)`, `nova(slot)`, `shatterNext()`, `overclock()`. The AI plays the rest. Captions\n  in the lower third name each feature as it happens (\"TURBO DUNK!\", \"ALLEY-OOP!\", \"SUPERNOVA!\"), plus \"DEMO · PRESS ANY\n  BUTTON\" (glyphs) blinking.\n- **Sound:** the attract plays music and effects at the user's volumes once audio has been unlocked (browsers allow\n  sound only after a gesture; before that it runs silently).\n\n---\n\n## 14. Dev mode (`46-dev.js`)\n\n**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item** (also `#dev` for tests; disabled in hub sessions). Choosing it resumes\nthe game with the **dev panel** docked on the right third of the screen. While the panel has the focus, the human\nplayers' slots are driven by CPU brains (the match keeps flowing, so every change shows live); Esc/○ or the pause key\ncloses the panel and gives control back. The panel is our own canvas UI (the same widgets as the menus), navigable by\npad, keys and mouse; one tab at a time, at most 8 rows a page.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| TUNING | every `TUNING` slider by group (Movement, Shooting, Dunks & Blocks, Defense, Supernova, CPU, Match, Physics, Courts), live; ← → or the mouse wheel change a value, △ resets one, RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS, SAVE AS MY DEFAULTS (`bb:tuning`), COPY AS JSON |\n| CHEATS | infinite turbo (P1 / everyone), always Supernova (HOME / AWAY), CPU passive, shots always in / always out / normal, unblockable dunks, one-shove knockdowns, big heads, power-ups every 5 s, twists on/off, freeze game clock, freeze shot clock, unlock everything, reset save data (asks first) |\n| MATCH | score ± for each team, quarter, clock, shot clock, give the ball to any slot, force a tip-off, end the quarter, end the game (win / loss), Supernova for any slot, shatter next dunk, spawn each power-up, place the Jackpot Spot, trigger each twist (gust, slicks, eruption, vent puff, Overclock, reboot), swap any slot to CPU or back |\n| SCENES | jump to: any court (Exhibition with chosen teams), any Tour stop, any story beat, credits, results, the attract mode (any segment), any Blam Camp lesson, the hub card preview, `#animlab`, `#shootaround` |\n| DEBUG | overlays: hitboxes (body radii, steal reach arcs, block hands, rim torus, backboard plane, ball), AI intents (text over each CPU: DRIVE, PASS→2, MARK #3, BOX OUT), shot chance at release (and the last shot's breakdown), ball path prediction, twist areas, event log (last 10 events), state snapshot |\n| TIME | game speed 0.1 / 0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2, freeze, step one frame (while frozen), slow motion on dunks on/off |\n| CAMERA | broadcast / high view, zoom, free camera (`cam.free`), reset |\n\nEvery slider shows its name, value, default and a one-line help text; changed values are marked with a dot.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Online: AI Hub (`50-hub.js`)\n\nFollows `vendor/hub-harness/README.md` (AI Hub Session Protocol v1). Outside a session (`AIHub.active` false, or\n`connect()` resolves `null`) the game is exactly the standalone game.\n\n### 15.1 Tags (in `<head>`, after the client script)\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other crew over two halves\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □/Space shoot · ✕/E pass · R2/Shift turbo · ○/Q shove\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\n\n### 15.2 The round: \"HUB SHOWDOWN\"\n\n- Straight into the round: no title, attract, menus or prompts. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode:\n  'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; build the match; `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start (no key press).\n- **Teams and seats:** seats 0 and 2 play for HOME, 1 and 3 for AWAY; empty slots are CPU (Pro). Teams and court come\n  from `AIHub.rng('roster')` (two different street crews; the court is HOME's), so every copy builds the same roster;\n  the host also sends it reliably once (`{ t: 'r', ... }`).\n- **Rules:** two halves of 1:30, a 3-s halftime card (no menus, no subs), power-ups and twists on, no cheats, no taunts\n  (they would be emotes). A tie at the end: 30 s of SUDDEN BLAM; still tied at time-up: a tie.\n- **Our own card** (until `start`): the court at night with both teams lined up; the hub's names over the players they\n  will control, in their seat colors, CPU over the rest; ready marks; how to win; this device's controls in its glyphs;\n  the countdown from the `card` event's `left` (PAUSED while `paused`). Enter, ✕ or a click on READY →\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △, the T key or a click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')` (again takes it back). Nothing\n  on the card changes the round.\n- **Start:** on `start`, show a 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()`; the host starts the tip-off when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n- **No pausing the world:** match scenes are not pausable in a session and `autoPause` is off; Options or Esc (Options\n  only while Create is not held: Create + Options is the hub's) opens a small session overlay that does not stop the\n  simulation: sound volume, voice volume, button symbols, close. No Quit, Restart or title.\n- **End:** the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` once, when the game ends or on `time-up`\n  (at once, within `graceMs`): winners' remaining human ids in the first array, losers' in the second (a tie: one\n  array); `scores`: each human's team score; `stats`: `{ id: { PTS, DUNKS, STL, BLK } }`; `awards`: Dunk of the Round,\n  Pickpocket, Wall. With one human player add `won: true | false`. Before `finish` the host sends a reliable last\n  snapshot with `over: 1`. On `end`: stop input, stop the music and voices, freeze, show the final score until the hub\n  removes the game.\n- **Leaving:** on `leave`, that seat's player becomes CPU at once and stays in the game; the round goes on. If the host\n  leaves, the hub voids the round: clients show \"HOST LEFT\" and wait for `end`.\n- **Server:** with `AIHub.server` true the host copy has no local player, camera, sound or input: it runs the world with\n  every human slot from the network, draws only a small \"HOSTING\" text, and does everything else a host does.\n- **Failure:** if the engine can't run (its boot reports an error), call `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n\n### 15.3 Netcode (host-authoritative)\n\n- **Host:** runs the whole match as usual; each human seat's slot uses a `NetSource` fed by that seat's input messages.\n  Its own player (when it has one) uses local input.\n- **Client → host**, every 66 ms (15/s), unreliable: `{ t: 'i', s: seq, a: AIHub.time(), m: [mx, my] (×64, integers),\n  h: heldBits, e: [[eventId, actionBit, down 1 | up 0], ...the last 8 edges] }`. The host applies the stick and held bits\n  and each edge event once (by id), in order, so a lost packet loses nothing.\n- **Host → all**, every 66 ms, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: seq, a: AIHub.time(), g: [phase, period,\n  clock×10, shot×10, scoreH, scoreA, possession, flags], b: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner, state], p: [[x, y, z, vx, vy,\n  facing×100, state, stateT×100, turbo×100, flags], ×4], ev: [[id, type, ...args] for events of the last second] }`.\n  Positions are rounded to integers.\n- **Clients** render remote things 100 ms in the past, interpolating between snapshots (snapping discrete states). Their\n  own player's running is predicted locally from its stick with the same movement code, and pulled toward the host's\n  position (blend 15% a frame; snap beyond 48; follow the host entirely during knockdowns, dunks, shots and other\n  non-running states). The ball, possession and every outcome come only from the host. Each event id plays its sounds,\n  captions and effects once.\n- **Budget:** at most 15 messages a second from each copy plus rare reliable ones (roster, over), under the client's\n  20/s limit; every message JSON and under 16 KB. If no snapshot arrives for 1 s, clients show \"WAITING FOR HOST\".\n- The host's tab hidden freezes the world (rAF stops); the hub voids the round after 20 s: accept it.\n\n### 15.4 What the harness checks (it must pass every scenario)\n\n`harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with\n`&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server`; use `&limit=45` to keep them short. It checks the tags, `connect`,\n`ready` with no key press, Enter on our card answering Ready, the start, traffic both ways, a server copy running the\nworld, a player leaving (with 3+ players the last one leaves), the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, every copy told\nthe round ended, no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets. Pass = `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` once\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`.\n\n---\n\n## 16. About/Credits and the exit interview\n\nThe About screen's pages (§11.4) and the final chat reply carry, as TASK.md requires (write \"unknown\" for anything not\nconfirmed):\n\n- **Source Information:** Date (TASK.md's: 2026-11-03 17:48:22); Source (\"Basketball, in the over-the-top arcade\n  style (genre inspiration; an original game)\"); Plan (`PLAN.md`); Genre and Perspective (arcade sports, 2-on-2\n  basketball; side-on broadcast camera, orthographic pitch 30°, optional High camera); Tech (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 modified,\n  AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node, Playwright 1.63, Python http.server for\n  tests); Art Direction; Animation; Audio; Online; Testing; Research; Environment (Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux;\n  browser unknown); Model (as TASK.md gives it, corrected if another model builds); Usage (estimates only if available).\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** the builder's answers to TASK.md's questions, in order.\n- **Credits:** the game; the engine (my-3D2dge, MIT); the AI Hub client; \"every sound, song and voice made in code\";\n  the engine changes (§5) with their reasons.\n\n`exit-interview.json` goes in the root beside the HTML, exactly in TASK.md's shape, plain text, every value filled, and\nchecked with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Its `aiHub` block:\nname `BASKETBLAM`, tagline `No fouls. No mercy. All BLAM.`, a one-to-two-sentence description, type `Game`, genre\n`Sports`, source `Basketball (over-the-top arcade style)`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags such\nas `[\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]`.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends with its tests passing (§19) and the game complete for what it contains: no menu entry, button or\nscreen for anything not built yet, no TODOs. Commit nothing outside the dev folder except the deliverables.\n\n| # | Milestone | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Pipeline | setup (§3); `tools/build.mjs` (fragments → `build/game.js`, `build/index.html`, the root bundle with the client first in `<head>`, `</script` escaped); `tests/run.mjs` and `helpers.mjs`; scenes table with a boot and an empty title; `game.debug` | `node tests/run.mjs` prints one line; the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors (`handoff/tools/check.mjs`) |\n| M1 | Court, ball, hoops, camera | the arena TileMap and the Skybox floor painter with lines; the broadcast view; hoop drawing (stanchion, cheated glass, rim halves, net springs); ball physics with rim, board, floor and walls; scoring detection; the camera director; `#shootaround` (a bench that fires seeded shots) | physics tests pass (made rate = decided rate ± 3%, no tunneling); screenshots of the ball in front of, inside and behind the net look right |\n| M2 | A playable 2-on-2 | player entity, the rig factory with shorts (engine change 1), movement and turbo, the dribble, possession, passes, jump shots with the release meter, 2/3 points, inbounds, both clocks, quarters, the match flow, a first CPU brain, HUD v1, `Cmd` and input sources, `serializeMatch`/`applySnapshot`, the event bus, tuning store | 1 player plays a whole game against the CPU on the Skybox; rules tests pass; a fake-hub test shows a second instance rendering the match from snapshots |\n| M3 | The arcade layer | layups, the 12 dunks with choreography and the dunk cam, alley-oops, putbacks, posterized, steals, shoves and knockdowns, spin moves, blocks, goaltending, rebounds and box-outs, the tip-off, Supernova, shatter and the sponsor break, juice and subs, stats and style points, banners and every effect (§9), `#animlab`, a first dev panel (TUNING with reset) | mechanics tests pass; filmstrips of every dunk, shove, block and celebration read well |\n| M4 | CPU AI | the full brains (§8), difficulty table, comeback, teammate commands, twist and power-up awareness | AI soak tests pass (§19); difficulty ordering holds |\n| M5 | Audio | every sound effect, the songs and stings, crowd ambience, the voice synth (engine changes 3 and 4) and the announcer system with captions | audio tests pass; in Chromium the audio smoke test finds sound and no errors |\n| M6 | Screens and flows | the UI kit, glyph icons and prompt lines, title, main menu, join (1–4), team select, lineup, court & rules, matchup card with codes, break cards, halftime report, results, Hall of Blam, How to Play, Options, About/Credits (with its text written as the build goes), touch-only notice, the themed pause menu and settings | flow and UI tests pass; screenshots at 1920×1080 and 390×844@3 read at a glance |\n| M7 | Content | the other four courts (floors, backdrops, silhouettes, props and new shapes, crowds, lights, weather) and their twists; all teams and rigs (engine change 2: hair); power-ups; the Jackpot Spot | content lint passes; an AI soak on every court; screenshots of each court |\n| M8 | Tour, story, camp | tour map, the prologue and every beat (§10.6), the boss mechanics, ending and credits, unlocks, autosave and CONTINUE TOUR, Hall of Blam entry, Blam Camp's 10 lessons | the scripted Tour playthrough and the camp tests pass |\n| M9 | Attract and dev mode | the attract director with its 5 segments, the full dev panel (§14) | attract and dev tests pass |\n| M10 | AI Hub | the card, host, client, server, leave, time-up, end, the session overlay | net tests and all four harness scenarios pass |\n| M11 | Finish | a balance pass with the dev sliders (scores of 30–60 per team in a 2:00-quarter game, about one dunk in three baskets, a Supernova most games), polish, a full screenshot review, the final bundle, About pages and the chat reply's sections, `exit-interview.json` | every test passes; the Definition of Done (§20) is all yes |\n\nOrder inside a milestone: data and rules first, then visuals, then tests that pin the behavior. Write each test with the\ncode it covers, and rerun a suite only after changing code it covers; run everything before closing a milestone.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shot and rim physics | balls tunnelling through the rim, odd bounces, made rates drifting from the decided chance | decide-then-fly (§6.7); 4× substeps near rims; the M1 `#shootaround` bench with hundreds of seeded shots checked against the decided outcome; tune `rimBounce` there |\n| Basketball animation on a procedural rig | IK hands that pop, dribbles out of sync, dunks that look stiff | the pose layer over `solvePose` with eased keys; dribble driven by the ball's own phase; `#animlab` and filmstrips from M2; clips are data, so iterate quickly |\n| Depth sorting around the hoop | ball, rim, net and glass drawn in the wrong order | split rim and net into back and front halves queued at different depths; screenshots of the ball at known positions (in front, inside, behind, on the rim) in M1 |\n| Backboards edge-on in an orthographic side view | an invisible glass, a weak look | the cheated, turned panel (§9.3), decided up front |\n| CPU that is dull, stuck or broken | the whole game rests on it | headless AI-vs-AI soaks on every court from M4 with stall detectors (shot clock violations, players not moving, nobody scoring) and difficulty-ordering checks |\n| Shared world over the hub | 20 messages a second, latency, loss, players leaving, a server copy | one `Cmd` path and snapshot functions from M2; a fake-hub test in M2; redundant edge events; small snapshots; the harness's four scenarios in M10 |\n| The standard pause stopping a hub round | the engine pauses on Start, on focus loss | in a session: `menu: false`, `autoPause: false`, unpausable scenes, our own non-pausing overlay (§15.2) |\n| Scope (5 courts, 22 rigs, a story) | running out of time with half-built content | data registries, a playable complete game by M3, content in M7 as data entries; never show what isn't built |\n| 10-foot readability and prompts | small text, wrong glyphs | the rules in §11.1; glyph unit tests per device and style; 1920×1080 screenshots |\n| Gibberish voice quality | it can sound like noise | formant pairs per vowel, per-character profiles, a seeded contour; listen in the browser once per profile; keep captions always on |\n| Touch-only detection | touchscreen laptops misdetected | require no fine pointer and no hover; switch back on a key press or a gamepad |\n| Determinism | engine internals use `Math.random` | gameplay draws from `S.rng`; tests seed `Math.random` too; the proof hashes twice |\n| The shared machine | ports and processes of other agents; a full /tmp | port 0 on 127.0.0.1, PID-only cleanup, `TMPDIR` inside the dev folder when needed |\n\n---\n\n## 19. Testing\n\n### 19.1 The one command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs [suite ...] [--quick]` (in the dev folder) runs the suites named, or all of them; `--quick` skips the\nbrowser and hub suites. It prints **only failures** (`FAIL <suite>.<test>: <what was expected, what happened, a short\nsnapshot>`) and then **one line**: `BASKETBLAM tests: 231 passed, 0 failed (41.8 s)`. Exit code 1 on any failure.\n\n- **Headless suites** load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `build/game.js` (and `vendor/aihub-session.js` first, as the page\n  does) into a fresh `node:vm` context with the stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`)\n  plus `removeEventListener`, `matchMedia` (configurable), `navigator` (`maxTouchPoints`, `getGamepads`) and a seeded\n  `Math.random`. They drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap / hold`, `game.addPlayer`,\n  `input.feed(...)` (mouse) and read `game.debug.snapshot()` and the event log.\n- **Bots:** a test \"plays\" a human seat by driving the real input actions from the CPU brain's own judgment (as\n  `kits/sports.js`'s `bot()` does), so the full input path is exercised.\n- Long runs use short quarters (`tune('quarterLength', 20)`), except one full-length game.\n\n### 19.2 Suites and what they check\n\n| Suite | Checks |\n|---|---|\n| `content` | every registry entry is valid: 6 teams × 3 players with 8 ratings in 1..10, rig specs, voices, taunts; 5 courts with every field; 12 dunks; 6 power-ups; 7 codes; line banks with ≥ 10 lines, ≤ 60 characters, only known slots; story beats name existing speakers; every setting has a default; every action has an icon on every device and style |\n| `physics` | floor bounce decay; 500 seeded \"made\" shots go in ≥ 97% and 500 \"missed\" ≤ 3%; banks off the glass; a 900 u/s ball never tunnels through rim or board; a basket counts only downward and once; the ball never leaves the arena |\n| `rules` | 2 vs 3 points by takeoff just inside / outside the arc and in the corners; dunk 2; goaltending awards the basket; Jackpot + 2; Gold Ball doubles; shot clock expiry is a turnover; a made basket gives the other team the inbound; the shot clock resets on rim contact; a release before the buzzer counts, after doesn't; overtime on a tie; SUDDEN BLAM after two; tip-off winner gets the ball; the alternating arrow for Q2–Q4 |\n| `mechanics` | turbo drain and refill; speed by ZOOM; steal rates by angle within expected bands over 1,000 seeded tries; shoves knock down and fumble; a spin move breaks steals and ankles; blocks succeed when timed and fail when late; layup vs dunk choice; dunk choice by distance and SLAM; alley-oop from pass to slam; putback; posterized; Supernova on after 3 straight, off after an opposing basket, 4 more baskets or 40 s; shatter → sponsor break → inbound; juice falls and subs apply; each power-up's effect and expiry; wind bends a shot but keeps its decided outcome; oil slicks slide and slip; lava bombs knock down; vents launch; Overclock at Q4; reboot after two knockdowns |\n| `ai` | 20 seeded CPU-vs-CPU games per court (20-s quarters): no errors; every team scores; scores in a sane band; ≤ 2 shot clock violations a game; no player still for more than 6 s of live play; across the batch the CPU dunks, shoots threes, steals, shoves, blocks, throws oops and uses power-ups; BLAM beats Rookie in ≥ 16 of 20 |\n| `flow` | boot → title; 10 s idle on the title, the main menu and the join screen → attract; a key, a pad button, a mouse click and a stick push each leave it in one step, back to the screen it interrupted with its choices intact; every main-menu entry reaches a working screen by keyboard, by pad and by mouse; Exhibition with 1, 2, 3 and 4 players (addPlayer) gives each the right player and side; pause shows Dev Mode, How to Play and (in a match) Restart; results' buttons work; Hall of Blam initials entry |\n| `tour` | **the scripted playthrough of the whole game**: a new Tour with a bot human, through the prologue, all three stops and the final, every beat seen in order, the reveal, the Overclock, the ending, credits, unlocks granted, Hall of Blam entry; it rematches a lost stop (exercising the loss path); CONTINUE TOUR after reloading the context mid-tour resumes at the right stop |\n| `camp` | every lesson completes with scripted input and saves its completion; skipping works; its prompts name the right keys or buttons per device |\n| `attract` | three full loops of every segment without errors; each segment's showcase events happen (event log); any input leaves within a step; touch-only: the loop continues and a tap shows the notice |\n| `dev` | the pause menu's Dev Mode opens the panel; each slider changes and clamps its value and the game reacts (e.g. `runSpeed` × 1.5 → 50% more distance in a second); RESET ALL restores every default; each cheat and match action works; every SCENES jump lands in its scene; overlays draw without errors (in the browser suite) |\n| `ui` | glyph icons for every action × keyboard, mouse, PlayStation and Xbox; prompts follow `lastDevice` per player; Button symbols changes every player's glyphs (and a later joiner's); settings defaults; touch-only detection on and off (stubbed `matchMedia` and `navigator`) and its switch-back on a key or gamepad |\n| `audio` | every song's tokens parse (no engine warnings); every sound name used exists; the voice's syllable plan for sample lines (count, timing, the \"!\" and \"?\" contours); no audio calls fail headless |\n| `net` | with `tests/fakehub.mjs` (2–4 game contexts sharing a simulated network with latency and loss, an `AIHub` stub per copy): clients' inputs move their players on the host; snapshots apply and the final scores agree; each event plays once; a leaver's player turns CPU; time-up → `finish` within the grace with valid standings; host leaving → clients show the void; server mode runs the world with no local player; every copy stays under 20 messages a second and unreliable messages under 1,200 bytes; the card answers Ready on Enter and More time on △ |\n| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same hash twice (the proof) |\n| `bundle` | the root HTML exists with the exact name; the client is the first script in `<head>`, byte-identical to `vendor/aihub-session.js`; the hub tags are there; no external URLs are loaded; its inline scripts run headless and reach the title |\n| `browser` (Playwright, `file://`) | `handoff/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle passes (no errors, the screen filled, look notes read and acted on); every deep link renders without errors; the audio smoke test (after a synthetic key press the AudioContext runs, a voice line and a song play without errors); the screenshot set below is written |\n| `hub` (Playwright + a 127.0.0.1 port-0 server) | the four harness scenarios of §15.4 pass; the server is checked to serve our page first and is stopped by its PID |\n\n### 19.3 Screenshots (for what scripts can't judge)\n\nWritten to `check-output/` by the browser suite at 1920×1080 (and 1280×720): the title; the main menu; join with 4\nplayers; team select; the matchup card; each court in play (5); a dunk at its apex with the dunk cam; a shatter; the\nSupernova trail; the hoop with the ball in front of, inside and behind the net; the halftime report; results; the tour\nmap; a story beat with portraits; the dev panel on each tab; the pause menu with Dev Mode; How to Play (pad and keyboard);\nAbout pages; the hub card; the touch-only title at 390×844@3. Look at every one: TV readability, the look target\n(§2), nothing clipped by the corner buttons. Filmstrips (`handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) for every dunk, the\nshove and knockdown, the block, the jump shot and the celebrations.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Definition of done (TASK.md, line by line)\n\n- [ ] The title is BASKETBLAM, from the RNG pick; the deliverable and the dev folder have TASK.md's exact names.\n- [ ] One self-contained HTML in the root; it runs from `file://` and inside the hub; no runtime network requests.\n- [ ] Built on the my-3D2dge handoff; engine changes marked and listed; the engine's native look and rig animation are\n      the base, with our new assets (courts, shapes, hoops, crowd, icons) and animations (§7).\n- [ ] All music, effects and voices made in code; voices are gibberish with captions.\n- [ ] AI Hub: tags, client first in `<head>`, own card, shared world, every harness scenario passing; the game unchanged\n      on its own.\n- [ ] Every system and mechanic in §6–§9 works; all content in §10 is in; every screen in §11 exists and works by pad,\n      keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device with PlayStation glyphs and an Xbox option.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu, with live sliders and reset to defaults, and the tools in §14.\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input leaves; it shows every feature.\n- [ ] Touch-only devices: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract running.\n- [ ] Narrative and announcer writing in the over-the-top arcade broadcast style (§10.6–10.7).\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders, stubbed features or dead menu entries (grep the source for TODO, FIXME, XXX, \"placeholder\").\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` passes, including the scripted playthrough of the whole Tour; screenshots reviewed.\n- [ ] The About/Credits screen and the final chat reply carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and\n      Prompt Feedback; `exit-interview.json` is beside the HTML, in TASK.md's shape, and parses.\n- [ ] Only processes you started were stopped, by PID; temporary folders removed.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A. Tuning defaults (`01-tuning.js`; every one a live dev slider)\n\n| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Movement | `runSpeed` | 108 | 60–160 | u/s before ZOOM |\n| | `accel` | 900 | 300–2000 | u/s² |\n| | `turboMult` | 1.5 | 1.0–2.2 | |\n| | `turboDrain` | 0.30 | 0.05–0.8 | per second held and moving |\n| | `turboRefill` | 0.20 | 0.05–0.8 | per second |\n| | `turboRefillDelay` | 0.35 | 0–1.5 | s |\n| | `playerGravity` | 900 | 500–1500 | |\n| | `jumpShotVz` | 250 | 150–400 | before SWAT |\n| Shooting | `shotSkill` | 1.0 | 0.4–1.6 | × every make chance |\n| | `threeSkill` | 1.0 | 0.4–1.6 | × three-point chance |\n| | `perfectWindow` | 0.10 | 0.03–0.30 | s, full width |\n| | `perfectBonus` | 0.15 | 0–0.4 | |\n| | `badReleasePenalty` | 0.30 | 0–0.6 | |\n| | `contestPenalty` | 0.40 | 0–0.8 | |\n| | `shotArc` | 1.0 | 0.6–1.6 | × apex height |\n| Dunks & blocks | `dunkRange` | 150 | 60–300 | from the rim, before SLAM |\n| | `dunkGravity` | 520 | 300–900 | |\n| | `dunkApex` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | |\n| | `dunkHang` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × flight time |\n| | `dunkSlowMo` | 0.45 | 0.1–1.0 | time scale at the apex (1 = off) |\n| | `blockReach` | 14 | 6–30 | before SWAT |\n| | `blockChance` | 1.0 | 0–2 | |\n| | `shatterChance` | 1.0 | 0–5 | |\n| Defense | `stealChance` | 0.30 | 0–0.9 | |\n| | `stealReach` | 18 | 8–36 | |\n| | `stealCooldown` | 0.6 | 0.1–2 | s |\n| | `shoveForce` | 220 | 60–500 | |\n| | `shoveCost` | 0.25 | 0–0.8 | turbo |\n| | `shoveCooldown` | 1.0 | 0.2–3 | s |\n| | `shoveFumble` | 0.6 | 0–1 | |\n| | `knockdownTime` | 0.8 | 0.2–2 | s |\n| | `spinCost` | 0.2 | 0–0.6 | turbo |\n| | `spinCooldown` | 1.5 | 0.3–4 | s |\n| Supernova | `novaBaskets` | 3 | 2–6 | to ignite |\n| | `novaMaxBaskets` | 4 | 1–10 | |\n| | `novaTime` | 40 | 10–120 | s of game clock |\n| | `novaShotBonus` | 0.25 | 0–0.6 | |\n| CPU | `cpuSkill` | 0 | −0.5–0.5 | offset on decision quality |\n| | `cpuReaction` | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | × reaction delays |\n| | `cpuAggression` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × steal and shove rates |\n| | `comeback` | 0.35 | 0–1 | |\n| Match | `quarterLength` | from the mode | 20–300 | s; the running match's (Exhibition 120, Tour 90, hub halves 90) |\n| | `shotClock` | 20 | 8–30 | s |\n| | `gameSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–1.5 | `game.timeScale` outside effects |\n| | `fatigue` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × juice loss |\n| Physics | `ballGravity` | 760 | 400–1200 | |\n| | `ballBounce` | 0.62 | 0.3–0.9 | |\n| | `rimBounce` | 0.45 | 0.2–0.8 | |\n| | `boardBounce` | 0.55 | 0.2–0.9 | |\n| Courts | `powerupInterval` | 22 | 6–60 | s |\n| | `hazardInterval` | 1.0 | 0.25–4 | × twist timers |\n| | `windStrength` | 140 | 0–300 | u/s² at full gust |\n| | `jackpotBonus` | 2 | 0–5 | points |\n\n## Appendix B. Data shapes\n\n```js\ndef('team', 'hightops', { name: 'NEON HEIGHTS HIGHTOPS', short: 'HIGHTOPS', colors: { jersey: '#ff3ca6', trim: '#2de2ff',\n  shorts: '#1a1420', sneaker: '#f4f4f4', sock: '#2de2ff' }, logo: LOGO_SNEAKER, court: 'skybox', locked: false,\n  players: ['volt', 'bigrumble', 'pixel'], captainLines: { /* §10.6 replies by opponent */ } });\ndef('player', 'volt', { name: 'VOLT', team: 'hightops', number: 7, role: 'high-flyer',\n  ratings: { zoom: 9, splash: 5, deep: 4, slam: 9, dime: 6, swipe: 6, swat: 4, bump: 3 },\n  rig: { build: 'heroic', size: 1.65, hair: 'ponytail', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#ff3ca6' }, skin: '#8a5a3c', hairColor: '#3ab0ff' },\n  voice: 'volt', taunt: 'raiseRoof', celebrations: ['raiseRoof', 'airplane', 'pointSky'], barks: ['Too slow!', 'Catch me!'] });\ndef('court', 'skybox', { name: 'THE SKYBOX', floor: paintAsphalt, lines: { main: '#2de2ff', paint: '#ff3ca6' },\n  logo: LOGO_SNEAKER, backdrop: { sky: [...], stars: 60, moon: {...}, layers: [...] }, silhouettes: drawSkyline,\n  props: [['fence-chain', 200, -40, { params: { len: 400 } }], ['streetlamp', -48, -24]], crowd: ['#ff3ca6', '#2de2ff', '#1a1a1a', '#ffd23a'],\n  ambient: .45, lights: skyboxLights, weather: null, dribble: 'dribble_asphalt', music: 'skybox', twist: 'jackpot' });\ndef('dunk', 'windmill', { banner: 'WINDMILL!', slam: 7, dist: [50, 150], hands: 1, spin: 0, flip: 0, apexAbove: 40,\n  keys: [[0, { R: [4, 2, 20] }], [.3, { R: [0, 7, 14] }], [.55, { R: [-4, 4, 36] }], [.8, { R: [3, 2, 46] }], [.9, { R: [8, 1, 30], slam: true }]],\n  bonus: 100, lines: 'dunkPower' });\ndef('lines', 'steal', ['PICKPOCKET! CHECK YOUR WALLETS, FOLKS!', '{NAME} SNATCHED IT LIKE A SEAGULL AT A FRY STAND!' /* ... ≥ 10 */]);\ndef('beat', 'reveal', { stage: 'dome-court', music: 'story', cast: ['gigawatt', 'dunkatron', 'swatbot', '{CAPTAIN}'],\n  lines: [['vinnie', 'THREE STOPS! THREE WINS! {TEAM} IS HEADED TO THE BLAM DOME!'], ['gigawatt', 'Congratulations...'] /* ... */],\n  camera: [[0, 'wide'], [2, 'gigawatt'], [5, 'bots']] });\ndef('powerup', 'rocket', { name: 'ROCKET KICKS', icon: ICON_ROCKET, color: '#ff7a2a', seconds: 15, apply(p) {...}, remove(p) {...} });\ndef('attract', 'seg4', { court: 'caldera', home: 'magma', away: 'hightops', seconds: 35, score: [22, 19], quarter: 3,\n  cheats: { infiniteTurbo: true, dunkRange: 220 }, script: [[6, 'twist', 'eruption'], [14, 'command', [0, 'vent']], [24, 'shatterNext']] });\n```\n\nA content lint (`content` suite) validates every entry at boot in dev builds and in tests, with messages that name the\nentry and the field.\n\n## Appendix C. A complete song in the engine's format (the `title` anthem)\n\n```js\nconst TITLE_SONG = { bpm: 108, steps: 4, tracks: [   // steps: 4 a beat, so a bar is 16 tokens\n  { name: 'bass', wave: 'square', vol: .22, notes:\n    'E2 . E3 . . E2 G2 . A2 . . B2 . A2 G2 . | E2 . E3 . . E2 G2 . D3 . C3 . B2 . G2 A2 |' },\n  { name: 'stabs', wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes:\n    '. . . . E4 . . . . . . . G4 - . . | . . . . E4 . . . . . . . A4 - B4 . |' },\n  { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes:\n    'k . h . s . h k . k h . s . h h | k . h . s . h k . k h . s h o . |' },\n  { name: 'hype', wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes:   // audio.layer('hype', 1, 1) after 8 bars\n    'B4 - - . A4 G4 . E4 - . . . . . . . | D5 - - . B4 A4 . G4 - . A4 . B4 - - . |' }\n] };\n```\n\nEvery other song follows this form (§12.1's table gives each one's feel, tempo, key and layers); check that the engine\naccepts each wave name and token (it warns on unknown ones) and listen to each in the browser once.\n\n*End of plan.*\n\n","numLines":406,"startLine":1200,"totalLines":1605}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PkMRLAkE9bLdYU5iw55emb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
