{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The /goal (set by the user): \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes, following PLAN.md and \"using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\"\n   - TASK.md overall: an original over-the-top arcade basketball game.\n     - The 10-foot UI must be controller-first, with PS glyphs by default and an Xbox option.\n     - Dev mode is reached from the pause menu, with live sliders and reset to defaults.\n     - An attract mode starts after 10 s idle, and any input exits it.\n     - Multiplayer through AI Hub.\n     - All audio is made in code, with gibberish voices.\n     - Touch-only devices show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button.\n     - No TODOs or placeholders.\n     - The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections go in both the chat reply and an in-game About screen.\n     - exit-interview.json uses the exact given shape.\n   - TASK.md constraints (verbatim, still in force): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Also: \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Tests must sit behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count.\n   - Git rule from the system context: commit or push only when the user asks; the user has not asked.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The my-3D2dge v0.85.2 engine:\n     - E.Game, scenes, the custom view `new E.View('broadcast','Broadcast',0,30,1,1)` registered as E.VIEWS.broadcast.\n     - E.TileMap with floorTex; E.Humanoid rigs with a pose layer wrapping `rig.solvePose` (E.ik3 IK).\n     - E.Dialog, E.Shell, E.Arcade, game.settings.\n     - Headless `game.advance` in node:vm.\n   - Engine pitfall: `game.after` timers are cleared on a scene change. This caused both the dev panel and hub bugs.\n   - Decide-then-fly shot model:\n     - Decided makes are \"ghost\" (no rim or board collision); rattles are cosmetic.\n     - Decided misses that would drop in are kicked out.\n   - Substepped rim-torus and backboard physics.\n   - Event bus `emit/on`; events carry `eid`, not `id`.\n   - Input sources: localSource, cpuSource (aiThink), netSource, scriptSource.\n   - AI Hub Protocol v1, shared-world, host-authoritative:\n     - Clients send inputs at 15/s.\n     - The host sends snapshots at 15/s.\n     - Clients interpolate 100 ms back and predict their own player.\n   - The Playwright `TMPDIR` must point into the dev folder, because the shared machine's /tmp is 100% full.\n   - The Shell is scaled with CSS zoom: `root.style.zoom = clamp(innerHeight/560, 1, 2.6)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Root (`.../work/`): TASK.md, STAGE.md and PLAN.md (read-only inputs); `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901.html` (the deliverable, about 1.7 MB); `exit-interview.json` (validated, parses; usage says ~2 h 10 min).\n   - Dev folder `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901/`:\n     - `engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the engine with changes marked `/* BASKETBLAM */`:\n       - shorts option on Humanoid (HD and classic);\n       - afro (drawn behind the face), flattop and mohawk hair;\n       - Dialog voice can be a function;\n       - `get sfxBus()` / `get musicBus()`.\n     - `tools/build.mjs`:\n       - concatenates `src/NN-*.js` into an IIFE in `build/game.js`;\n       - writes `build/index.html` (dev page), `build/hub/game.html` with copies of the harness, and the root single file;\n       - the client script comes first in `<head>`, followed by the hub tags;\n       - NAME = 'Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901'.\n     - `src/`, in fragment order:\n       - 00-core (constants: OX=64, OY=64, CW=640, CH=288; RIMS; KEYS including tabL/tabR/more; GAME_SETTINGS; game; S; emit/on; def/get/all);\n       - 01-tuning (TUNING plus sliders);\n       - 02-data-teams (6 teams plus hidden camp team, 18 players plus intern1-3, CAST, LOGOS via mkLogo);\n       - 03-data-courts, 04-data-story, 05-data-lines;\n       - 06-data-moves (CLIPS, 12 dunks, power-ups, CODES);\n       - 08-data-about (ABOUT_PAGES with final feedback text plus a TITLE provenance line; SECRETS_TEXT);\n       - 10-audio-music (SONGS, STINGS, playMusic, sting, musicLayer);\n       - 11-audio-sfx (SFX including bomb_hit; sfx());\n       - 12-audio-voice (planSyllables, Voice with vol .32 default and robots ×1.7, announcer and captions, crowd bed plus DE-FENSE chant);\n       - 20-court-build (3-tier stands, MAP_H=25, floor painters, new shapes);\n       - 21-court-draw (ARENA, hoops, crowd, silhouettes, jumbotron, cleaning bot, lava moat, rim glow);\n       - 22-twists;\n       - 30-ball;\n       - 31-player (Baller; infTurbo: 'all' / 'p1' / 'team');\n       - 32-anim (pose layer, dribble, drawPlayer);\n       - 33-actions;\n       - 34-ai (handler/defense/loose AI; orders: dunk, quake, vent, jumper, putback, shove, steal, block; passiveT after a reboot);\n       - 35-match (auto-inbound for a human after 2.5 s; endAfterDead buzzer handling);\n       - 36-fx (camera in real-time slow-mo windows; High view zoom ×.56);\n       - 37-match-scene;\n       - 40-ui-kit (glyphs, navInput, screenFrame with menuBackdrop);\n       - 41-hud, 42-screens, 43-tour, 44-camp, 45-attract, 46-dev (LAB / animlab, shootaround);\n       - 50-hub, 90-start (scenes, pauseItems, Shell with zoom fit, boot, deep links, game.debug, window.__bb exports).\n     - Most recent edit, `src/50-hub.js`:\n       ```js\n       game.go('match', { match: o }, { fade: 0 });   // (matchEnter calls hubAssignSources once the match exists)\n       }\n       function hubAssignSources() {\n         for (const [slot, seat] of Object.entries(NET.slotSeat)) {\n           const p = S.players[+slot]; if (!p) continue;\n           p.human = [0, 2, 1, 3].indexOf(+slot);\n           if (+slot !== NET.mySlot && NET.role !== 'client') p.source = netSource(+seat);\n         }\n       }\n       ```\n     - `src/37-match-scene.js` matchEnter, after `S.lesson = FLOW.lesson || null; FLOW.lesson = null;`: `if (HUB && NET.info) hubAssignSources();`. It also handles FLOW.openDev.\n     - `tests/`: `run.mjs` (17 suites; sets TMPDIR to `.test-tmp` and removes it), `helpers.mjs`, `core.test.mjs`, `play.test.mjs`, `net.test.mjs`, `web.test.mjs` (bundle / browser / hub).\n       - net.test now checks that the host source is 'net', that both copies tag the humans, and that client input moves the host player more than 60 units (match forced live/practice).\n     - `tools/verify-browser.mjs`: real keys; dev mode slider and reset; attract mode.\n     - `tools/verify-audio.mjs`: analyser RMS and centroid; writes `check-output/audio-sample.webm`.\n     - `tools/verify-settings.mjs`: Camera High and Xbox through the Settings UI; uses one browser context.\n     - `tools/verify-hub-manual.mjs`: the harness driven by hand (written with the Write tool, because the heredoc triggered a safety check).\n     - Temporary folder `.verify-tmp` still exists (holding TMPDIR and helper scripts `rows.mjs`, `two.mjs`, `ls.mjs`); it must be removed.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Settings apply functions referenced `game` before initialization; fixed by using the `g` parameter.\n   - Unknown prop 'bench'; changed to `shape:bench`.\n   - The font lacks `·`, `◂` and `✓`; replaced with `•`, `←`/`→` and `★`.\n   - Logo overlap; fixed with a measured layout.\n   - Event `id` was overwritten by the bus; renamed the bus field to `eid`.\n   - Balance:\n     - First soak: 100 points per team and 91% dunks.\n     - Fixed with handler/defense AI rework, an oop cooldown of 12 s, and a dunk block base of .34.\n     - Result: about 50 per team and 43–55% dunks.\n   - Physics:\n     - Rattles bounced out; made all decided makes ghost and the rattle cosmetic.\n     - Misses dropped in; added an in-and-out kick.\n     - Wind crossing issue; target z set to RIM_Z-.5 and rattle offset 2.5.\n     - The `scored` flag is now reset in giveBall.\n   - Buzzer-beater skipped the quarter end; fixed with endAfterDead.\n   - Slow-mo windows in game time stretched themselves; switched to `game.real`.\n   - Human-inbounder hang; auto-inbound after 2.5 s, and the CPU no longer defers.\n   - Lesson chaining cleared by scene exit; the lesson now passes via FLOW.lesson.\n   - Double step completion crash; fixed with a `waiting` flag.\n   - The nova lesson reset heat; added an init hook.\n   - The jumper lesson spot was behind the arc; moved it to (470,110).\n   - Attract showcases: added toSpot/make/jumper, grant, toVent, nearRim; defensive orders are handled first.\n   - Dev panel did not open via `game.after`; now uses FLOW.openDev.\n   - Pause menu too small; Shell zoom added, and the duplicate Help was removed.\n   - Python http.server buffered its output; now run with `-u`, and the server is killed via its spawn handle.\n   - Leftover server stopped by PID after checking `/proc/pid/cwd`.\n   - Chromium crashed because /tmp was full; TMPDIR is set inside the dev folder.\n   - High camera too zoomed in; zoom ×.56.\n   - Voices too quiet; raised.\n   - Hub remote players were CPU-driven (`game.after` cleared); fixed with hubAssignSources in matchEnter.\n   - Stop hook feedback 1: title, audio, and dev/attract not checked in a browser. I did the browser verifications, measured and recorded audio, and kept the plan's title with an explanation.\n   - Stop hook feedback 2: title RNG not done in-session, audio not listened to, High camera / Xbox / harness not checked by hand, need a line-by-line audit. I added the title provenance on the About page, verified High and Xbox via the Settings UI, drove the harness manually, found and fixed the hub bug, and still intended to write an audit.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All suites passed previously: 2,360 checks.\n   - After the hub fix, `node tests/run.mjs net` gives 31 passed, 0 failed.\n   - The manual harness confirmed:\n     - P2's Enter answered ready (ready [1]);\n     - Start now led to a live match;\n     - P2 holding A moved its host player from x 386 to 261;\n     - removing P3 turned only slot 1 CPU;\n     - Time up led to finish with standings [[0,1],[2]], and copies were told the round ended.\n   - Title: I kept BASKETBLAM per STAGE.md and PLAN §1 (\"Do not re-pick it\"; RNG `secrets.randbelow(50)` returned 18 at the planning stage); this is documented on the About page.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The /goal command text quoted in section 1.\n   - Stop hook feedback 1: \"Not satisfied... 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' is not shown. TASK.md asks for a 50-title brainstorm with a real RNG pick, and the transcript shows the title was taken from PLAN.md with no brainstorm or RNG run. The transcript also shows no check that the dev-mode slider and attract-mode requirements were met in the browser beyond automated suites, and the audio was never listened to. The 'no TODOs, placeholders or stubs' check was only run via a grep in tests against src, and the About pages were rewritten with placeholder-like text... The title-selection requirement is the clearest unmet item.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback 2: \"The bundled HTML exists, exit-interview.json parses, and the final reply has all four sections. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. TASK.md asks for a fifty-title brainstorm with a real RNG pick; the transcript shows only that the plan recorded one, and no brainstorm or RNG run was done in this session. The assistant itself says it 'still can't hear the audio' and that the audio was only measured, not listened to, and it did not check the High-camera, Xbox glyph setting, or AI Hub real-harness behaviour beyond automated runs. The 'no TODOs, placeholders or stubs' check relied on grep plus automated tests, which is weaker than a line-by-line feature audit.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Rebuild (already done after the hub fix) and run the full `node tests/run.mjs` to confirm everything is green after the hub change.\n   - Write a line-by-line TASK.md feature audit, e.g. `AUDIT.md` in the dev folder, mapping each TASK.md requirement to its implementation and evidence (tests, real-browser scripts, screenshots).\n   - Remove the temporary folder `.verify-tmp`.\n   - Make sure no started servers remain.\n   - Update the usage/session time if needed in `exit-interview.json` and the About page (and rebuild if the About page changes).\n   - Give the final reply containing all four sections:\n     - Source Information, with the title provenance;\n     - Testing Feedback, updated to add the hub CPU-source bug found by manual harness driving; the critical count may rise to 8;\n     - Engine Feedback;\n     - Prompt Feedback.\n   - In the final reply, explain the title decision and honestly state that I cannot hear audio but measured it and saved a recording.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was addressing stop hook feedback 2.\n   - verify-settings.mjs confirmed: Camera→High gives view 'threequarter'; Button symbols→Xbox persists to a fresh page as `shoot:xbox:2 pass:xbox:0 shove:xbox:1 oop:xbox:3 turbo:xbox:7`; no page errors.\n   - verify-hub-manual.mjs found that remote hub players were CPU-controlled. I fixed this with `hubAssignSources()` called from matchEnter.\n   - I tightened net.test: the host source must be 'net', both copies tag the humans, and client input must move the host player more than 60 with the match forced live.\n   - The last command, `node tests/run.mjs net`, gave \"BASKETBLAM tests: 31 passed, 0 failed\".\n   - The manual harness rerun showed P2's player moving 386→261 and sources [\"local\",\"cpu\",\"net\",\"cpu\"].\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run the full suite (`cd` into the dev folder; `node tests/run.mjs`) to confirm that all ~2,360 checks pass after the hub fix. Then write the line-by-line TASK.md audit file, remove `.verify-tmp`, and give the final reply with the Source Information, Testing Feedback (including the newly found hub bug), Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections. This responds to the latest hook feedback: \"it did not check the High-camera, Xbox glyph setting, or AI Hub real-harness behaviour beyond automated runs. The 'no TODOs, placeholders or stubs' check relied on grep plus automated tests, which is weaker than a line-by-line feature audit.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-060901--x5a4f79-work/5ad0c147-1