{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LJj7uPJNEuCkjGt3cp6Sg3","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901/AUDIT.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad0c147-1299-4fc9-adba-2f06893c3033","uuid":"07d78c37-9b17-4713-8877-6ca7f6b1489b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:31:11.608Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060901__x5a4f79/work/Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901/AUDIT.md","oldString":"| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | | tests `bundle` (source scan); a scan of `build/game.js` and the shipped HTML finds no TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\" |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and an in-game About/Credits | About pages (`08-data-about.js`): Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Engine Changes, Secrets | `#about`; final reply |","newString":"| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | Every feature above has its code path and is reached in tests or the browser scripts; content counts in the built game: 53 tuning sliders (9 groups), 12 songs, 8 stings, 58 effects, 23 voices, 406 announcer lines in 52 banks, 14 new shapes, 12 dunks, 22 celebrations, 6 power-ups, 10 lessons, 5 courts | tests `bundle` (source scan); a scan of `build/game.js` and the shipped HTML (engine and hub client included) finds no TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\", lorem |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and an in-game About/Credits | About pages (`08-data-about.js`): Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Engine Changes, plus Secrets once the bots are beaten | `#about`; final reply |","originalFile":"# BASKETBLAM: TASK.md, line by line\n\nEach requirement in TASK.md and where it is met. \"Tests\" names a check in `node tests/run.mjs` (17 suites); \"browser\"\nnames a script in `tools/` that drives the shipped HTML in Chromium with real key presses and clicks.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Where it is met | How it was verified |\n|---|---|---|\n| SOURCE: basketball, over-the-top arcade style | An original 2-on-2 arcade basketball game: turbo, impossible dunks, legal shoves, Supernova hot streak, two hype announcers (`src/33-actions.js`, `35-match.js`, `36-fx.js`) | tests `mechanics`, `ai`; screenshots `check-output/shot-*.png` |\n| Genre: picked to fit | Arcade sports (2-on-2), with a story ladder (Tour), Exhibition, tutorial (Camp) | About page, exit-interview |\n| Perspective: picked to fit | Side-on broadcast camera (`BROADCAST`, pitch 30) with dunk cam; Settings > Camera > High (three-quarter view) | browser `verify-settings.mjs` (Camera > High through the Settings screen; `check-output/verify-high.png`) |\n| Game Title: a riff on the name, 50 brainstormed, picked with a real RNG | BASKETBLAM. Picked at the planning stage exactly as TASK.md says: 50 riffs brainstormed, Python `secrets.randbelow(50)` returned 18 (PLAN.md section 1, which says not to re-pick); STAGE.md directs \"using the title it gives\" | PLAN.md lines 40-42; About > Source Information records it |\n| Research: optional | None beyond the engine handoff docs and the hub README | About, exit-interview |\n| Package: one HTML named `GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901.html` | `../Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901.html`, self-contained (client, engine, game inlined; no network) | tests `bundle` (exact name, no external loads, runs headless to the title) |\n| Tech stack: built on my-3d2dge `dist/handoff`, free to change it | `engine/my-3d2dge.js` (v0.85.2) with 4 marked changes (`/* BASKETBLAM: ... */`): shorts, hair styles, Dialog voice function, public audio buses | `grep BASKETBLAM engine/my-3d2dge.js`; About > Engine Changes |\n| Art: engine's native style as base, new assets for the source | 5 code-painted court floors with lines and logos (`20-court-build.js`), hoops (angled glass, split rim, spring net), crowds, silhouettes, 14 new prop shapes, team logos, power-up icons, glyph icons; engine props for generic items | screenshots of each court; tests `content` (shapes registered) |\n| Animation: engine's system as base, new animations | Pose layer over `rig.solvePose` (two-bone IK hands): dribble synced to the ball, jump shot, layup, passes, steal, shove, spin, block, rebound, 12 dunk choreographies, hang on the rim, 20+ celebrations and taunts (`32-anim.js`, `06-data-moves.js`) | `#animlab`; filmstrip `check-output/lab-strip.png` |\n| Audio: all in code, gibberish voices | 12 songs + 8 stings (`10-audio-music.js`), ~60 effects (`11-audio-sfx.js`), formant gibberish voices for 23 speakers + crowd bed (`12-audio-voice.js`) | tests `audio`; browser `verify-audio.mjs` measures the master output (levels, spectra per voice) and saves `check-output/audio-sample.webm` for a listener |\n| Online: ai-hub `lib/hub` | Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0 first in `<head>`, own card, shared world (`50-hub.js`) | tests `net` (fake hub), `hub` (the harness's 4 scenarios); browser `verify-hub-manual.mjs` (card Enter = Ready, Start now, a client's keys move its player on the host, Remove player turns it CPU, Time up finishes) |\n| Dev folder named `GameTitle-SOURCE-...`, modules bundled into the root HTML | `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901/` with `src/` fragments, `tools/build.mjs` | the folder; tests `bundle` |\n| Shared machine: read only what is needed; port 0 on 127.0.0.1, check the page, stop only own processes by PID | Servers: `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, title checked, stopped through their own process handle; browser temp files kept in the dev folder because the shared /tmp was full | tests `hub`; `verify-hub-manual.mjs` |\n| Performance unlimited | Canvas lighting on every court, ~260 animated fans, particles, weather, afterimages | screenshots |\n| Testing: headless tools, scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a count | `node tests/run.mjs` prints failures and one line; tests `tour` plays the whole Tour through the real inputs | `BASKETBLAM tests: N passed, 0 failed` |\n| Goal: an original game inspired by the source | Own teams, courts, characters, story (no real teams or likenesses) | content |\n| Scope: feature-complete demo, all features and mechanics shown, infrastructure for the rest | Tour (4 stops + story), Exhibition (any teams and courts, 1-4 players), Camp (10 lessons), Hall of Blam, How to Play, Options, About; content as data registries (`def/get/all`), tuning table, dev tools | tests `flow`, `tour`, `camp`; About |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, standard tools, live sliders for the important variables, reset to defaults | Pause > Dev Mode opens a panel: TUNING (53 sliders in 9 groups, reset one, RESET ALL, save, copy JSON), CHEATS, MATCH, SCENES, DEBUG overlays, TIME, CAMERA (`46-dev.js`) | tests `dev`; browser `verify-browser.mjs` (Esc, Dev Mode, slider 108 to 128: the player runs 128 instead of 102 in a second, RESET ALL, Esc closes) |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menu, looping AI demo, any input exits, may cheat | 5 scripted CPU segments forcing every showcase, cards, Hall of Blam, logo; loops (`45-attract.js`) | tests `attract` (3 loops, every showcase event, any input leaves), `flow` (title, menu, join; key, pad, click, stick); browser `verify-browser.mjs` (11 s idle on the title, a key returns) |\n| Multiplayer: per ai-hub, and the game on its own | Local 1-4 (join screen, keyboard halves, pads); AI Hub sessions 1-4 | tests `flow` (2, 3, 4 players on their sides), `net`, `hub` |\n| Narrative tone like the source | 90s broadcast hype: announcer banks (~400 lines), story beats, sponsor breaks, halftime gags (`04`, `05`) | tests `content` (caps, length, slots) |\n| 10-foot, controller-first; PS DualSense standard mapping | Square shoot, Cross pass, R2/R1 turbo, Circle shove, Triangle oop, L1 taunt; Options opens Settings; 5x7 font at scale 1+, focus outline + pointer + pulse, prompt bar on every screen | tests `ui`; screenshots at 1920x1080 |\n| Keyboard and mouse native | WASD/arrows, Space/J shoot, E/K pass, Shift turbo, Q/L shove, F/I oop, R/U taunt; mouse: hover moves focus, click picks, right click backs, wheel turns sliders; in play left click shoots, right click passes | tests `flow` (mouse click leaves attract, menu by keyboard and pad); browser `verify-browser.mjs` |\n| Prompts follow the last device; PS glyphs; Settings option for Xbox; keys and mouse buttons for KB&M | `glyphFor` / `promptLine` (`40-ui-kit.js`), Settings > Button symbols | tests `ui`; browser `verify-settings.mjs` (Button symbols > Xbox through the Settings screen, kept after a reload: How to Play shows X A B Y RT LB; `check-output/verify-xbox.png`) |\n| No dense web-style data screens | Big buttons, at most ~7 items a group, cards with portraits; box score is 4 rows x 6 numbers | screenshots |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract runs | `detectTouchOnly` (`90-start.js`), title notice and SETTINGS button, attract tap shows the notice | tests `attract`, `ui`; screenshot `shot-touch-only.png` at 390x844@3 |\n| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | | tests `bundle` (source scan); a scan of `build/game.js` and the shipped HTML finds no TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\" |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and an in-game About/Credits | About pages (`08-data-about.js`): Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Engine Changes, Secrets | `#about`; final reply |\n| exit-interview.json beside the HTML, exact shape, parses | `../exit-interview.json` | `node -e \"JSON.parse(...)\"`, every field filled |\n\nKnown limits, stated plainly: the audio was measured and recorded, not listened to by ear; browser checks ran in\nChromium only; usage (cost, tokens) is not visible inside the session.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":8,"newStart":31,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | Prompts follow the last device; PS glyphs; Settings option for Xbox; keys and mouse buttons for KB&M | `glyphFor` / `promptLine` (`40-ui-kit.js`), Settings > Button symbols | tests `ui`; browser `verify-settings.mjs` (Button symbols > Xbox through the Settings screen, kept after a reload: How to Play shows X A B Y RT LB; `check-output/verify-xbox.png`) |"," | No dense web-style data screens | Big buttons, at most ~7 items a group, cards with portraits; box score is 4 rows x 6 numbers | screenshots |"," | Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract runs | `detectTouchOnly` (`90-start.js`), title notice and SETTINGS button, attract tap shows the notice | tests `attract`, `ui`; screenshot `shot-touch-only.png` at 390x844@3 |","-| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | | tests `bundle` (source scan); a scan of `build/game.js` and the shipped HTML finds no TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\" |","-| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and an in-game About/Credits | About pages (`08-data-about.js`): Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Engine Changes, Secrets | `#about`; final reply |","+| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | Every feature above has its code path and is reached in tests or the browser scripts; content counts in the built game: 53 tuning sliders (9 groups), 12 songs, 8 stings, 58 effects, 23 voic