{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CpMbUwGwT9uqXneGesniX1","type":"tool_result","content":"7:Game Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901.html]. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share thi\n42:Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game. \n82:    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n83:    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n---\nRead TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how to build it, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort) in this folder. Build the game TASK.md describes, following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\n---\n1. **Every possession can end in spectacle.** Dunks, blocks, shoves and steals are big, readable and loud.\n2. **Simple buttons, real timing.** Four main buttons; skill lives in release timing, turbo management, alley-oop\n   timing and steal angles.\n3. **Personality everywhere.** Two hype announcers, trash talk, courts with twists, a crowd that reacts.\n4. **Couch first, 10 feet away.** Up to four on one screen, a TV-readable HUD, controller-first menus.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Title, names and folders\n\n- **Title: BASKETBLAM.** Picked as TASK.md asks: fifty riffs on \"basketball\" were brainstormed and one was chosen with a\n  real random number generator (Python `secrets.randbelow(50)` returned 18). Do not re-pick it.\n- **SOURCE token** in file names: `Basketball`.\n- **Names for this TASK.md** (copy them exactly):\n  - dev folder: `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174822/` (in the root, beside TASK.md)\n  - deliverable: `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174822.html` (in the root)\n  - exit interview: `exit-interview.json` (in the root, beside the HTML)\n\n  If your TASK.md names another model or timestamp, use your TASK.md's names with the same `Basketblam` and\n  `Basketball` tokens.\n- **Dev folder layout:**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad0c147-1299-4fc9-adba-2f06893c3033","uuid":"76389ffa-9427-48fe-b161-fa1a71164f60","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:39:07.871Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"7:Game Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901.html]. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060901].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need - other ag